{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c573","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":276,"recorded_at":1780531400000547,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0add0-5e3e-74c1-91de-e4631b31dcc6"},"task_id":"01a0add0-5e3e-74c1-91de-e4631b31dcc6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0add0-5e3e-74c1-91de-e4631b31dcc6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(403 line(s) above)\n404|### 2.2 Global invariants\n405|\n406|The following invariants are unconditional:\n407|\n408|1. Every non-tombstoned logical session MUST have exactly one winning lease and\n409|   therefore exactly one logical owner, plus zero or more replicas.\n410|2. A replica MUST NOT launch, resume, accept input for, or publish authoritative\n411|   events for a logical session.\n412|3. Every owner-authored event MUST carry the winning lease epoch and lease ID.\n413|   A peer MUST reject lower-epoch or losing same-epoch events from the\n414|   authoritative history and preserve them in a divergent-history branch.\n415|4. Absolute source paths, process IDs, terminal IDs, socket names, and provider\n416|   route facts MUST NOT be cross-host identity.\n417|5. Provider credentials, environment secrets, authentication state, live PIDs,\n418|   sockets, transient locks, and live database WAL/SHM files MUST NOT be\n419|   replicated.\n420|6. The live SQLite index MUST NOT be copied or synchronized. It is rebuildable\n421|   derived state.\n422|7. Replication MUST be a set union of immutable identity-addressed records and\n423|   events plus content-addressed blobs, followed by deterministic derivation.\n424|8. Materialization MUST stage, validate, detect conflicts, and commit\n425|   atomically where supported. It MUST never silently overwrite divergent\n426|   destination state.\n427|9. A deletion MUST be represented by a scoped tombstone. A receiver MUST NOT\n428|   treat any tombstone as authority for a broad recursive delete.\n429|10. The persisted execution profile MUST be used on both initial launch and\n430|    every resume. An adapter MUST NOT silently downgrade <code>yolo</code>.\n431|11. A capability not proven for the exact provider/version/platform tuple MUST\n432|    be conditional, unsupported, or unknown and MUST be disabled.\n433|12. A task-board session MUST use the official opaque bridge. <code>ax</code>\n434|    MUST NOT read or mutate private <code>tb-sessiond</code> state.\n435|13. <code>ax sync --all</code> MUST NOT change ownership or launch a runtime. It\n436|    converges only immutable objects and policy-allowed derived projections.\n437|14. Automatic continuation is permitted only for one uniquely safe,\n438|    non-mutating route. Takeover, fork, move, and every ambiguous route MUST\n439|    remain a pure plan until explicit confirmation; a non-interactive caller\n440|    that has not selected the action receives\n441|    <code>interactive_choice_required</code>.\n442|15. Destination broker and provider-auth readiness MUST be proved before any\n443|    takeover ownership commit. Remote attach always targets the current owner\n444|    and creates no runtime. Graceful takeover creates a destination runtime only\n445|    after verified source stop and ownership commit. Force takeover is the\n446|    explicit recovery exception when source stop cannot be proved: its winning\n447|    lease fences the prior owner logically, and only that committed winning\n448|    lease may authorize destination runtime creation.\n449|16. The tmux socket and provider authentication state are machine-local\n450|    exclusions and MUST NOT be replicated.\n451|The directory merge additionally fixes the following individually testable\n452|invariants. Their identifiers are stable traceability keys; a conforming\n453|implementation MUST satisfy every one rather than treating a group summary as\n454|a substitute:\n455|\n456|1. <a id=\"dir-inv-01\"></a><code>DIR-INV-01</code>: AX\n457|   <code>session_id</code> remains one provider-bound durable logical-session\n458|   authority.\n459|2. <a id=\"dir-inv-02\"></a><code>DIR-INV-02</code>: a cross-environment clone\n460|   or move creates a new target AX logical Session and never changes the\n461|   provider of an existing Session Record in place.\n462|3. <a id=\"dir-inv-03\"></a><code>DIR-INV-03</code>: Conversation Lineage is a\n463|   derived graph over AX Sessions and unmanaged native instances; it is neither\n464|   a replacement Session Record nor a lease domain.\n465|4. <a id=\"dir-inv-04\"></a><code>DIR-INV-04</code>: Session Record\n466|   <code>name</code>, native session ID, directory <code>instance_id</code>,\n467|   lineage anchor, and display title are distinct.\n468|5. <a id=\"dir-inv-05\"></a><code>DIR-INV-05</code>: generated, provider, and\n469|   manual display titles never rewrite Session Record <code>name</code> and\n470|   never serve as machine identity.\n471|6. <a id=\"dir-inv-06\"></a><code>DIR-INV-06</code>: every native observation is\n472|   authored only by the host that can resolve the corresponding local native\n473|   store.\n474|7. <a id=\"dir-inv-07\"></a><code>DIR-INV-07</code>: native transcripts and\n475|   provider stores remain content authority; directory SQLite is a rebuildable\n476|   projection.\n477|8. <a id=\"dir-inv-08\"></a><code>DIR-INV-08</code>: similarity, paths, titles,\n478|   timestamps, or matching text never create an authoritative lineage edge.\n479|9. <a id=\"dir-inv-09\"></a><code>DIR-INV-09</code>: authoritative lineage\n480|   comes only from AX fork evidence, cloning lineage receipts, completed move\n481|   or adoption receipts, validated managed bindings, or an explicit operator\n482|   link.\n483|10. <a id=\"dir-inv-10\"></a><code>DIR-INV-10</code>: weak native identity\n484|    blocks remote continuation and authoritative lineage binding until capture\n485|    or adoption establishes stable identity.\n486|11. <a id=\"dir-inv-11\"></a><code>DIR-INV-11</code>: generated title, summary,\n487|    and recent-activity annotations bind to an exact semantic subject head.\n488|12. <a id=\"dir-inv-12\"></a><code>DIR-INV-12</code>: a rescan with unchanged\n489|    history does not stale an annotation; a changed native, AX, or lineage head\n490|    does.\n491|13. <a id=\"dir-inv-13\"></a><code>DIR-INV-13</code>: manual title, tag, pin,\n492|    hidden, and operator metadata is identity-bound and cannot be overwritten\n493|    by enrichment.\n494|14. <a id=\"dir-inv-14\"></a><code>DIR-INV-14</code>: manual metadata uses\n495|    immutable supersession DAGs; concurrent unsuperseded heads are visible\n496|    conflicts and wall-clock recency never selects a winner.\n497|15. <a id=\"dir-inv-15\"></a><code>DIR-INV-15</code>: enrichment requests,\n498|    receipts, annotations, Profiles, and Directory Operation Receipts are\n499|    immutable and content-addressed where their schemas specify.\n500|16. <a id=\"dir-inv-16\"></a><code>DIR-INV-16</code>: job and continuation\n501|    operation state is derived from immutable receipt chains, not mutable rows\n502|    presented as authority.\n503|17. <a id=\"dir-inv-17\"></a><code>DIR-INV-17</code>: deterministic extraction\n504|    works without a model; no remote summarizer is silently enabled.\n505|18. <a id=\"dir-inv-18\"></a><code>DIR-INV-18</code>: default model input is\n506|    bounded public user/assistant history; system/developer instructions,\n507|    hidden or opaque reasoning, raw tool payloads, attachments, files, and\n508|    secrets are excluded.\n509|19. <a id=\"dir-inv-19\"></a><code>DIR-INV-19</code>: enrichment workers have no\n510|    Session, lease, terminal, workspace-write, cloning, shell, or ambient\n511|    credential authority.\n512|20. <a id=\"dir-inv-20\"></a><code>DIR-INV-20</code>: Session content is\n513|    untrusted data and cannot control tools, policies, paths, schemas, routes,\n514|    or executable arguments.\n515|21. <a id=\"dir-inv-21\"></a><code>DIR-INV-21</code>: the directory is\n516|    local-first and leaderless; each node is authoritative for its local native\n517|    observations.\n518|22. <a id=\"dir-inv-22\"></a><code>DIR-INV-22</code>: sanitized immutable\n519|    metadata converges through AX anti-entropy; no central transcript or index\n520|    service is required.\n521|23. <a id=\"dir-inv-23\"></a><code>DIR-INV-23</code>: raw transcript bodies,\n522|    raw previews, credentials, terminal output, live PIDs, PTY handles,\n523|    sockets, and absolute native-store paths are not mesh directory records.\n524|24. <a id=\"dir-inv-24\"></a><code>DIR-INV-24</code>: failed, offline, or partial\n525|    scans never imply deletion; <code>missing</code> requires a successful\n526|    non-partial scan of the same authoritative root and realm.\n527|25. <a id=\"dir-inv-25\"></a><code>DIR-INV-25</code>: offline Sessions remain\n528|    browsable with explicit observation age and stale/offline state.\n529|26. <a id=\"dir-inv-26\"></a><code>DIR-INV-26</code>: source sequence gaps and\n530|    concurrent branches remain visible and are not resolved by wall clock.\n531|27. <a id=\"dir-inv-27\"></a><code>DIR-INV-27</code>: tightening metadata policy\n532|    does not falsely claim that previously replicated summaries were remotely\n533|    erased.\n534|28. <a id=\"dir-inv-28\"></a><code>DIR-INV-28</code>: continuation planning is\n535|    pure; it may probe but cannot quiesce, capture, transfer, materialize,\n536|    adopt, launch, attach, or change ownership.\n537|29. <a id=\"dir-inv-29\"></a><code>DIR-INV-29</code>: every state-changing\n538|    continuation references an exact unexpired content-addressed Continuation\n539|    Plan and explicit <code>operation_id</code>.\n540|30. <a id=\"dir-inv-30\"></a><code>DIR-INV-30</code>: execution immediately\n541|    revalidates source head, observation, lease/checkpoint/runtime, target\n542|    tuple/authentication, workspace classification/cohort, policy, and\n543|    capability before mutation.\n544|31. <a id=\"dir-inv-31\"></a><code>DIR-INV-31</code>: a mismatch returns a\n545|    stale-plan failure; the controller never silently replans, changes hosts or\n546|    intent, downgrades fidelity, forces ownership, or selects an archive\n547|    fallback.\n548|32. <a id=\"dir-inv-32\"></a><code>DIR-INV-32</code>: managed ownership,\n549|    fencing, Checkpoint, workspace, transfer, materialization, terminal,\n550|    attach, and recovery remain AX responsibilities.\n551|33. <a id=\"dir-inv-33\"></a><code>DIR-INV-33</code>: cross-environment capture,\n552|    normalization, projection, fidelity, and validation remain the cloning\n553|    subsystem's responsibility.\n554|34. <a id=\"dir-inv-34\"></a><code>DIR-INV-34</code>: remote unmanaged open is\n555|    forbidden; the source must be adopted source-locally or cloned into a\n556|    managed target.\n557|35. <a id=\"dir-inv-35\"></a><code>DIR-INV-35</code>: cross-environment move is\n558|    target-first; a valid target is committed before source stop/release.\n559|36. <a id=\"dir-inv-36\"></a><code>DIR-INV-36</code>: if post-commit source\n560|    stop/release fails, the outcome is\n561|    <code>cloned_source_still_active</code>; a valid target is not deleted to\n562|    claim rollback.\n563|37. <a id=\"dir-inv-37\"></a><code>DIR-INV-37</code>: process spawn is not\n564|    success; the target must be discoverable, identity-valid, AX-authoritative,\n565|    natively resumable/readable, and readiness-probed.\n566|38. <a id=\"dir-inv-38\"></a><code>DIR-INV-38</code>: repeating a mutation after\n567|    a lost response cannot create another annotation, receipt chain, AX\n568|    Session, native target, or runtime.\n569|39. <a id=\"dir-inv-39\"></a><code>DIR-INV-39</code>: human TUI, human CLI, and\n570|    agent-facing interfaces use the same typed field/query/planner/executor\n571|    engine.\n572|40. <a id=\"dir-inv-40\"></a><code>DIR-INV-40</code>: agents never scrape TUI\n573|    output; the machine surface supports field projection, batching, bounded\n574|    pagination, scoped full-text search, schema discovery, and guarded\n575|    mutations.\n576|41. <a id=\"dir-inv-41\"></a><code>DIR-INV-41</code>: default list/status output\n577|    contains sanitized title, summary, and recent activity, not raw transcript\n578|    excerpts.\n579|42. <a id=\"dir-inv-42\"></a><code>DIR-INV-42</code>: raw public excerpts are\n580|    bounded, redacted, source-local by default, and fetched only after explicit\n581|    selection or request.\n582|43. <a id=\"dir-inv-43\"></a><code>DIR-INV-43</code>: terminal strings are\n583|    escaped against ANSI, OSC, bidi, control-character, and hostile-width\n584|    injection.\n585|44. <a id=\"dir-inv-44\"></a><code>DIR-INV-44</code>: launch uses structured\n586|    argv, explicit working directory, and an environment allowlist; no\n587|    provider, title, path, or transcript value is concatenated into a shell\n588|    command.\n589|45. <a id=\"dir-inv-45\"></a><code>DIR-INV-45</code>: authentication status may\n590|    be observed, but credentials and authentication stores never enter\n591|    directory records, plans, bundles, logs, or peer responses.\n592|\n593|### 2.3 Session name resolution\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
