{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5a5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":301,"recorded_at":1780531400000597,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0add0-6ac6-74e1-9e5f-d680eb1b3ef0"},"task_id":"01a0add0-6ac6-74e1-9e5f-d680eb1b3ef0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0add0-6ac6-74e1-9e5f-d680eb1b3ef0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1907 line(s) above)\n1908|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1909|\n1910|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1911|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1912|\n1913|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1914|| --- | --- | --- |\n1915|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1916|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1917|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1918|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1919|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1920|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n1921|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n1922|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n1923|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n1924|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n1925|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n1926|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n1927|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n1928|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1929|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1930|\n1931|The object is closed; every row is required, including nullable fields.\n1932|Normative example:\n1933|\n1934|~~~json\n1935|{\n1936|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:lease\",\n1937|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1938|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:8ead987abed8c7c05175b447c9a0e2b3a521f12e5a989acb8abe132576852d63\",\n1939|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1940|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1941|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1942|  \"epoch\": 4,\n1943|  \"holder_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1944|  \"predecessor_lease_id\": \"bbbbbbbb-cccc-4ddd-8eee-ffffffffffff\",\n1945|  \"reason\": \"graceful_takeover\",\n1946|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1947|  \"issued_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1948|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1949|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:00.000Z\",\n1950|  \"extensions\": {}\n1951|}\n1952|~~~\n1953|\n1954|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n1955|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n1956|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n1957|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n1958|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n1959|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n1960|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n1961|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n1962|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n1963|\n1964|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n1965|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n1966|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n1967|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n1968|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n1969|\n1970|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n1971|\n1972|- accepting operator input after attach;\n1973|- starting a provider turn;\n1974|- publishing a checkpoint;\n1975|- pushing records or workspace changes; and\n1976|- resuming after any transport or sleep interruption longer than the configured\n1977|  lease refresh interval.\n1978|\n1979|There is no time-expiring ownership lease in v0.5.0. Liveness is not authority.\n1980|A host being offline does not make a replica owner; only a takeover or fork\n1981|does.\n1982|\n1983|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n1984|\n1985|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n1986|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n1987|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
