{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":322,"recorded_at":1780531400000639,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0add0-75ad-7f20-9672-26a64c9e2557"},"task_id":"01a0add0-75ad-7f20-9672-26a64c9e2557","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0add0-75ad-7f20-9672-26a64c9e2557","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1353 line(s) above)\n1354|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1355|\n1356|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1357|\n1358|| Operation | Required result |\n1359|| --- | --- |\n1360|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1361|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1362|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1363|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1364|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1365|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1366|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1367|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1368|\n1369|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1370|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1371|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1372|or unverified.\n1373|\n1374|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1375|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1376|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1377|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1378|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1379|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1380|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1381|as identity.\n1382|\n1383|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1384|\n1385|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1386|managed pane MUST run:\n1387|\n1388|~~~shell\n1389|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1390|~~~\n1391|\n1392|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1393|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n1394|tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or\n1395|used as cross-host migration.\n1396|\n1397|AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse\n1398|the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server\n1399|creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a\n1400|credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n1401|or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and\n1402|its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n1403|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST\n1404|NOT fall back to direct server creation.\n1405|\n1406|<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance\n1407|requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate\n1408|provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact\n1409|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1410|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1411|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1412|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1413|\n1414|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1415|\n1416|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1417|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1418|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1419|   materialization is valid;\n1420|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1421|   interactive terminal; or\n1422|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1423|\n1424|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1425|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1426|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1427|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1428|NOT authorize resume.\n1429|\n1430|### 4.3 Native Windows backend\n1431|\n1432|Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with\n1433|Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and\n1434|provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote\n1435|attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force\n1436|takeover, stop, and continuation.\n1437|\n1438|Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the\n1439|live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,\n1440|which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.\n1441|Terminal scrollback and live process memory are not portable state.\n1442|\n1443|Full tmux restore on a Windows computer is a WSL2 feature and uses the Linux\n1444|paths, process model, and provider installation inside that distribution. A\n1445|native Windows provider store and a WSL2 provider store are distinct\n1446|materialization targets.\n1447|\n1448|### 4.4 User services\n1449|\n1450|The background service integration is:\n1451|\n1452|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n1453|- a systemd user unit on Linux and WSL2 where systemd is enabled;\n1454|- otherwise an explicitly installed per-user periodic launcher on WSL2; and\n1455|- a Scheduled Task or per-user service on native Windows.\n1456|\n1457|The service MAY run periodic sync, peer health checks, tombstone\n1458|acknowledgement, stale-process detection, and wrapper restoration. Core commands\n1459|MUST work without it. Service absence MUST degrade freshness, not corrupt\n1460|ownership.\n1461|\n1462|The macOS launchd background control plane and Aqua terminal broker are separate\n1463|roles. The control plane MUST NOT acquire GUI/Keychain authority by proxy and\n1464|MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. The Aqua broker exposes\n1465|only authenticated, same-user, generation-bound terminal readiness and server\n1466|operations; it does not gain lease, workspace, provider, or replication\n1467|authority.\n1468|\n1469|## 5. Domain records and state machine\n1470|\n1471|### 5.1 Session Record\n1472|\n1473|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1474|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1475|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1476|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1477|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1478|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1479|\n1480|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1481|| --- | --- | --- |\n1482|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1483|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
