{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":343,"recorded_at":1780531400000681,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0add0-7f3b-78a1-9d35-1235392038e2"},"task_id":"01a0add0-7f3b-78a1-9d35-1235392038e2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0add0-7f3b-78a1-9d35-1235392038e2","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(9252 line(s) above)\n9253|### 13.6 Graceful takeover\n9254|\n9255|Command form is <code>ax takeover NAME --to HOST</code>; <code>--to</code>\n9256|defaults to the local host in interactive use.\n9257|\n9258|Preconditions:\n9259|\n9260|- source is reachable and proves it holds the winning lease;\n9261|- destination is allowlisted, is not the source, and has compatible contracts;\n9262|- destination provider/platform capabilities required by the session are\n9263|  available;\n9264|- on macOS, the destination Aqua broker, dedicated AX tmux server generation,\n9265|  functional sentinel, and separate provider-auth smoke are current for the\n9266|  selected provider build and macOS version;\n9267|- workspace-group members can all be quiesced or separated into worktrees;\n9268|- one exact WorkspaceGroupExpectation and Section 12.6 workspace mode have\n9269|  been selected;\n9270|- destination conflicts are absent or already resolved;\n9271|- task-board bridge is available for a task-board session; and\n9272|- no other takeover operation is active for the session.\n9273|\n9274|Transitions:\n9275|\n9276|1. Destination allocates one group operation ID and one session operation ID\n9277|   for each migration-cohort member. It calls <code>handoff.prepare</code> for\n9278|   each, naming the identical WorkspaceGroupExpectation, source lease,\n9279|   destination host, expected source checkpoint, and MaterializationCohort whose\n9280|   two arrays both equal the selected migration cohort. A single-member cohort\n9281|   still carries the exact expectation and one-element arrays.\n9282|2. Source blocks new input and changes <code>running|idle</code> to\n9283|   <code>quiescing</code>.\n9284|3. Through <code>handoff.quiesce</code>, source calls provider or task-board\n9285|   quiesce and waits for a complete safe boundary. A task-board source uses\n9286|   bridge <code>export --mode handoff</code>, requires\n9287|   <code>BridgeSafeBoundary.safe = true</code>, maps it exactly to RPC and\n9288|   checkpoint evidence, and retains its source-control token. Timeout or an\n9289|   incomplete bridge proof fails closed.\n9290|4. Source captures a fresh checkpoint under the current lease. A direct source\n9291|   uses the Section 7.5 Object Sink path for a portable provider snapshot or a\n9292|   validated zero-entry identity manifest for a backend-only provider; a\n9293|   task-board source uses only the opaque bundle. Both use the exact Section\n9294|   10.4 workspace-group root.\n9295|5. Source performs the final bulk record/blob/workspace/board sync to\n9296|   destination.\n9297|6. Destination stages, validates, and conflict-checks every referenced object.\n9298|   It does not resume. Destination broker and provider-auth readiness MUST be\n9299|   proved before ownership commit; a diagnostic Aqua manager name or sentinel\n9300|   alone is not proof.\n9301|7. Destination calls <code>handoff.stop</code>. Source requests graceful\n9302|   provider/task-board stop, verifies process exit and durable-store closure,\n9303|   and records <code>session.stopped</code>. A task-board source consumes the\n9304|   bridge source-control token with bridge <code>stop</code>.\n9305|8. If normal exit appended provider/manager closure records, source captures a\n9306|   closure-only delta, creates a superseding validated checkpoint, and syncs\n9307|   that delta. Any unexpected workspace/background mutation fails the graceful\n9308|   flow while the source remains the stopped owner.\n9309|9. Destination calls tagged <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9310|   <code>intent = ownership_transfer</code>, the exact non-empty selected cohort\n9311|   in both cohort arrays, and kind workspace/provider/task-board/composite from\n9312|   the checkpoint sources. It then performs atomic materialization through RPC\n9313|   <code>materialize.commit</code>, which leaves a durable rollbackable prepared\n9314|   transaction; a direct portable-store path invokes provider\n9315|   <code>materialize</code> inside it. For task-board, destination also performs\n9316|   the journaled Section 10.6 import/open sequence inside commit, never before\n9317|   prepare. No prepared path accepts input.\n9318|10. After every migration-cohort member is stopped/prepared and group\n9319|   expectation still matches, destination creates each member's epoch\n9320|   <code>source_epoch + 1</code>, predecessor source\n9321|   lease, reason <code>graceful_takeover</code>, and checkpoint from step 4.\n9322|   When step 8 created a superseding checkpoint, that checkpoint replaces the\n9323|   step-4 checkpoint in this lease.\n9324|   Destination persists each lease, then calls <code>handoff.commit</code> so source and\n9325|   destination union and persist that Lease Record. Destination MUST verify it\n9326|   is still the winning lease after union; if a concurrent higher/winning lease\n9327|   exists, it MUST NOT adopt or resume.\n9328|11. For a direct session, destination validates native discovery and resumes\n9329|    through <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> with the checkpoint-derived\n9330|    effective profile and new fencing token, using plugin <code>resume</code>.\n9331|    For task-board, destination performs no out-of-band adopt or resume.\n9332|12. After exact direct process status proves the owner resumed, destination\n9333|    invokes <code>materialize.finalize</code> with\n9334|    <code>direct_owner_resumed</code>, the effective profile, and its source\n9335|    event. For task-board, it invokes finalize with\n9336|    <code>task_board_owner_resumed</code>; finalize consumes the journaled open\n9337|    token, adopts the exact binding, resumes with that profile, and proves\n9338|    bridge status. Finalize commits any provider transaction and removes\n9339|    rollback bytes. A lost response is recovered with\n9340|    <code>materialize.status</code>.\n9341|13. Source becomes a replica, its wrapper parks, and destination publishes\n9342|    <code>lease.transferred</code> and <code>session.resumed</code> for every\n9343|    moved member. The resumed event repeats the exact effective profile/source\n9344|    used by finalize. Whole-group mode reports all affected session IDs; separate-\n9345|    worktrees mode reports only the selected session.\n9346|\n9347|Failure and recovery are phase-specific:\n9348|\n9349|| Failure boundary | Authority | Required recovery |\n9350|| --- | --- | --- |\n9351|| Before source stop | Source lease remains owner and process MAY be unquiesced; destination staging is inert | Abort handoff, resume source input, or retry same operation |\n9352|| After source stop, before destination lease | Source remains logical owner but is stopped; destination is a replica | Retry materialization, resume source, or restart takeover from the same checkpoint |\n9353|| After destination lease is persisted | Destination is owner; source MUST NOT resume | Retry destination adopt/resume; a failed pre-resume prepared transaction may roll back destination bytes while authority stays at destination; if activation remains impossible, gracefully transfer back from stopped state or perform explicit force recovery |\n9354|| After provider resume/finalize but before response | Destination lease plus provider and materialization status decide success, not the lost client response | Retry operation ID; inspect provider/bridge and <code>materialize.status</code>; do not create another epoch or guess rollback |\n9355|\n9356|No failure before step 10 MAY advance ownership. No failure after step 10 MAY\n9357|allow the old source to resume.\n9358|Before step 10, abort recovery MUST use <code>handoff.abort</code> so the source\n9359|records whether it unquiesced or remained stopped. After step 10,\n9360|<code>handoff.abort</code> MUST refuse because ownership recovery requires a new\n9361|lease transition.\n9362|\n9363|### 13.7 Force takeover\n9364|\n9365|Force takeover is an explicit recovery operation:\n9366|\n9367|~~~shell\n9368|ax takeover NAME --to HOST --force --expect-owner HOST_ID --expect-epoch EPOCH\n9369|~~~\n9370|\n9371|Interactive use MUST display that the old process can still exist, split-brain\n9372|history can result, and both histories will be preserved. Non-interactive use\n9373|MUST include destination, both expected values, and <code>--yes</code>.\n9374|\n9375|Force takeover MUST NOT claim or require a verified source-process stop. It is\n9376|the explicit exception to the graceful stop-before-commit sequence because the\n9377|source may be unreachable and its old process may still exist. Destination\n9378|realm and provider-auth readiness MUST be proved before the force lease is\n9379|persisted. Only the winning committed force lease authorizes destination\n9380|runtime creation; its fencing token rejects the prior owner from authoritative\n9381|sync or resume, and the old process MAY continue until it observes that losing\n9382|lease and parks or stops. This exception does not weaken the readiness-before-\n9383|ownership or runtime-after-ownership requirements.\n9384|\n9385|Preconditions:\n9386|\n9387|- destination is allowlisted and not known to hold a losing lease;\n9388|- the operator supplies/accepts the observed owner and epoch;\n9389|- the newest available checkpoint is integrity-valid; and\n9390|- destination materialization is either conflict-free or explicitly directed\n9391|  to a new copy/worktree;\n9392|- one exact WorkspaceGroupExpectation and Section 12.6 workspace mode are\n9393|  selected; whole-group mode has a recovery checkpoint for every migration\n9394|  member;\n9395|- the complete Session Record, provider identity, and persisted profile are\n9396|  available; and\n9397|- no local process is using the proposed destination native-store/workspace\n9398|  paths.\n9399|\n9400|A direct session additionally requires an accepted <code>native_resume</code>\n9401|tuple and one of two exact recovery bases: an accepted\n9402|<code>portable_store</code> plan, or a provider probe proving that the\n9403|destination's machine-local authenticated backend already resolves the exact\n9404|Provider Identity Record without copied store bytes. Required destination\n9405|credentials remain machine-local. The terminal backend and profile mapping\n9406|MUST pass before lease advance.\n9407|\n9408|A task-board session additionally requires bridge protocol 1.0.0 with\n9409|status/import/open/adopt/resume, an integrity-valid opaque bundle from the\n9410|selected checkpoint, and destination-local board/provider authentication. A\n9411|local board requires its staged <code>.task-board</code> tree and a successful\n9412|standalone <code>task-board validate</code>; a remote board requires access to\n9413|the exact logical board identity. <code>ax</code> MUST NOT substitute a whole-\n9414|board archive or inspect private manager state.\n9415|\n9416|Common pre-lease preparation and fencing are:\n9417|\n9418|1. Allocate one group operation and one takeover <code>operation_id</code> per\n9419|   migration member; attempt best-effort lease refresh and sync. Lack of source\n9420|   contact is not fatal. Every member uses the same WorkspaceGroupExpectation\n9421|   and MaterializationCohort with both arrays equal to the selected recovery\n9422|   cohort.\n9423|2. Preserve local destination divergence as an independent checkpoint or\n9424|   select a new copy/worktree. Select one immutable source checkpoint and pin\n9425|   all referenced object IDs.\n9426|3. Stage and validate workspace state without mutating the destination. For a\n9427|   direct session, also stage the accepted provider plan or prove exact backend\n9428|   identity resolution. For task-board, validate the opaque bundle and bridge\n9429|   capability/authentication only; bridge import/open is forbidden until\n9430|   <code>materialize.prepare</code> has durably created the transaction journal\n9431|   and fresh staging authority. No pre-lease staging accepts input.\n9432|4. Re-run membership, conflict, disk, terminal, provider/bridge,\n9433|   authentication, and profile\n9434|   checks. Any failure through this step aborts with the observed lease still\n9435|   authoritative. Staging and dormant state remain inert and may be retried or\n9436|   garbage-collected by their token-expiry rules.\n9437|5. Display/require the split-brain confirmation. Persist a machine-local\n9438|   confirmation receipt bound to operation ID, expected owner/epoch,\n9439|   checkpoint, destination, and all three accepted risks.\n9440|6. In whole-group mode, require all member confirmations and validated inert\n9441|   object staging before selecting each <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code>.\n9442|   Provider and task-board materialization journals do not yet exist. Create a\n9443|   new random lease ID with reason <code>force_takeover</code> and that member's\n9444|   selected checkpoint, and durably persist it. In separate-worktrees mode this\n9445|   applies only to the selected session. Ownership MUST NOT advance before\n9446|   steps 1–5 pass for the full selected cohort.\n9447|7. Recompute the winner after every reachable peer response. If this lease has\n9448|   already lost, do not materialize, adopt, or resume. If it wins, emit\n9449|   <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> followed by\n9450|   <code>lease.forced</code> under the new lease; the former must exactly match\n9451|   the receipt and accepted-risk tuple in Section 5.2.\n9452|\n9453|The direct path then MUST:\n9454|\n9455|1. invoke tagged RPC <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9456|   <code>intent = ownership_transfer</code>, the exact selected non-empty cohort,\n9457|   and provider/composite kind as workspace participation requires, then invoke\n9458|   <code>materialize.commit</code> to enter a rollbackable prepared\n9459|   workspace transaction and, only when <code>portable_store</code> is\n9460|   available, invoke plugin <code>materialize</code> inside it with the new\n9461|   fencing token;\n9462|2. validate native discovery of the exact Provider Identity Record, or validate\n9463|   exact authenticated-backend resolution for a backend-only identity;\n9464|3. fail with <code>unsupported_backend_identity</code> or\n9465|   <code>native_store_conflict</code> rather than create or relabel a blank\n9466|   provider session; and\n9467|4. call plugin <code>resume</code>, launch the returned plan through\n9468|   <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>, revalidate the lease before input, and\n9469|   prove the process is the exact native session; and\n9470|5. invoke RPC <code>materialize.finalize</code> with\n9471|   <code>activation = direct_owner_resumed</code>, the checkpoint-derived\n9472|   effective profile/source, recover a lost response through\n9473|   status, and only then publish <code>session.resumed</code>.\n9474|\n9475|The task-board path then MUST:\n9476|\n9477|1. invoke tagged RPC <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9478|   <code>intent = ownership_transfer</code>, the exact selected non-empty cohort,\n9479|   and task-board/composite kind as workspace participation requires, then enter\n9480|   a rollbackable prepared transaction. Commit performs the exact journaled\n9481|   bundle installation, bridge import, and dormant open; for a local board, run\n9482|   standalone <code>task-board validate</code> again against prepared bytes;\n9483|2. call <code>materialize.finalize</code> with\n9484|   <code>activation = task_board_owner_resumed</code>, the exact new binding,\n9485|   and checkpoint-derived effective profile/source. The coordinator consumes\n9486|   its journaled open token, adopts, verifies status, resumes, verifies status,\n9487|   and commits transaction cleanup;\n9488|3. publish <code>task_board.adopted</code> and\n9489|   <code>session.resumed</code> from the recovered finalize result, exactly\n9490|   once and with the same effective profile/source; and\n9491|4. never access the manager record, provider snapshot, or goal binding except\n9492|   as opaque bridge/bundle data.\n9493|\n9494|On later union, all peers apply the deterministic lease rule. The prior owner\n9495|becomes stale, while losing-lease events and checkpoints remain in divergent-\n9496|history branches for reconciliation.\n9497|\n9498|Failure and recovery are path- and phase-specific:\n9499|\n9500|| Boundary | Authority and required recovery |\n9501|| --- | --- |\n9502|| Any direct capability, identity, store-plan, or staging failure before step 6 | No new lease exists. Abort safely, retain resumable staging when useful, and leave the observed owner unchanged. |\n9503|| Any task-board authentication, bundle, or board-validation failure before step 6 | No new lease exists and no bridge import/open has occurred. Discard inert staging or retry from the immutable bundle. No blank manager/provider session may be opened. |\n9504|| New force lease loses before activation | The deterministic winner owns. Roll back every prepared host/provider transaction, leave task-board state dormant, and park this destination. |\n9505|| Direct materialization/native-discovery failure after step 6 | Destination remains the stopped or failed owner. Use RPC rollback, which consumes the provider rollback token internally, retain staging/history, and retry the same operation or perform a newer explicit takeover. Never roll ownership back. |\n9506|| Task-board commit/import/open fails after step 6 | Destination remains the stopped owner. Recover the journal with status or roll back pre-adopt bytes; a new prepare may allocate fresh bridge sub-operation IDs only after the prior transaction is terminal. |\n9507|| Task-board open token expires after step 6 but before adopt | Destination remains the stopped owner. Roll back the terminal pre-adopt transaction, then prepare/import/open the same immutable bundle in a new materialization; never reuse the staging root or mutate the old journal. |\n9508|| Task-board adopt returns no response | Recover <code>materialize.status</code>, which reconciles bridge status. Exact binding continues; no binding retries the same adopt ID while its token is valid; another binding is <code>lease_conflict</code>. Never inspect private state or guess. |\n9509|| Task-board adopt succeeds but resume fails | Destination is the adopted, stopped/failed owner. Retry finalize/bridge resume with the same persisted IDs; do not roll back bytes, unadopt, restore the old owner, or replace it with a blank provider session. |\n9510|| Provider/bridge or materialization finalization response is lost | Lease, terminal/bridge status, provider transaction status, and RPC <code>materialize.status</code> decide the result. Retry by operation ID and do not create another epoch or guess rollback. |\n9511|\n9512|The following sequence fixtures are normative. They start with source A at\n9513|epoch 4, destination B as replica, and checkpoint C4 unless a row says the\n9514|pre-lease gate fails:\n9515|\n9516|| Fixture | Required phase trace | Required terminal authority/state |\n9517|| --- | --- | --- |\n9518|| <code>FT-DIRECT-POS</code> | stage workspace/store or backend proof → validate identity/profile → confirm → persist B epoch 5 → prepare → commit/prepared → discover exact native identity → resume → finalize/committed | B epoch 5 running; A stale after convergence; force-confirmed and lease-forced events precede resumed |\n9519|| <code>FT-DIRECT-PRE-NEG</code> | direct capability or backend identity check fails before confirmation/fencing | A epoch 4 unchanged; B has inert staging only; no force audit event or epoch-5 lease |\n9520|| <code>FT-DIRECT-POST-NEG</code> | persist B epoch 5 → prepared materialization/native discovery fails → provider then host rollback | B epoch 5 stopped/failed; A stale after convergence; no resumed event and no blank native session |\n9521|| <code>FT-TB-POS</code> | validate bundle/auth → confirm → persist B epoch 5 → prepare journal/fresh root → commit/import/open dormant → finalize/adopt/resume | B epoch 5 running and adopted; A stale; adoption event precedes resumed |\n9522|| <code>FT-TB-AUTH-NEG</code> | destination board/provider authentication fails before import/open | A epoch 4 unchanged; no manager activation, force event, or epoch-5 lease |\n9523|| <code>FT-TB-TOKEN-NEG</code> | persist B epoch 5 → commit/import/open dormant → token expires before adopt | B epoch 5 stopped; roll back pre-adopt transaction, then prepare/re-import/re-open same bundle; authority never rolls back |\n9524|| <code>FT-TB-ADOPT-UNKNOWN</code> | adopt response is lost → status returns exact binding, null, or different binding | Exact continues to resume; null retries dormant adopt; different fails lease conflict; B remains owner after epoch 5 |\n9525|| <code>FT-TB-RESUME-NEG</code> | adopt exact binding → bridge resume fails | B epoch 5 adopted and stopped/failed; retry resume only; no unadopt, A resume, or blank substitution |\n9526|\n9527|If two force takeovers choose the same epoch, bytewise greater lease ID wins.\n9528|The loser MUST stop accepting input when it learns the winner. If destination\n9529|cannot resume after acquiring the lease, it remains the stopped/failed owner;\n9530|recovery is retry, graceful transfer from stopped state, or a newer explicit\n9531|force takeover. Ownership MUST NOT roll back implicitly.\n9532|\n9533|### 13.8 Fork\n9534|\n9535|<code>ax fork NAME --from CHECKPOINT --as NEW_NAME [--to HOST]</code> defaults\n9536|to the newest validated checkpoint; destination defaults to local only in\n9537|interactive use. Non-interactive use MUST supply <code>--to</code>.\n9538|\n9539|Preconditions:\n9540|\n9541|- checkpoint and all referenced objects are available and valid;\n9542|- NEW_NAME is unused;\n9543|- destination workspace conflict policy is satisfied;\n9544|- provider <code>fork</code> can produce a new native identity or a sanitized\n9545|  new-session plan; and\n9546|- task-board supports bundle open in <code>fork</code> mode when applicable.\n9547|\n9548|Transitions:\n9549|\n9550|1. Allocate a caller-stable fork operation ID, a new logical session ID, a new\n9551|   workspace-group ID, a fresh workspace ID for every source topology member,\n9552|   and an epoch-1 lease owned by the destination. No source ID is reused.\n9553|2. Derive and validate the exact Section 10.5 ForkWorkspaceProjection. Persist\n9554|   the complete new Workspace Group Record and every re-identified destination\n9555|   Transfer Manifest before publishing any object that refers to them. Source\n9556|   topology/manifests remain byte-identical.\n9557|3. Derive the effective execution profile and nullable profile-source event\n9558|   from the selected source checkpoint. Create the new Session Record with that\n9559|   profile, the new group/member IDs, and required core\n9560|   <code>fork_provenance</code>; persist it and its epoch-1 lease. A failure\n9561|   before this point leaves only unreferenced immutable projection objects and\n9562|   no logical fork.\n9563|4. For a direct session, invoke the side-effect-free provider <code>fork</code>\n9564|   planning operation with the fork operation ID. For\n9565|   <code>supported_import</code>, call <code>native-store-plan</code> in\n9566|   <code>mode=fork</code> before prepare and validate its provider component;\n9567|   <code>native_fork</code> has no provider-store component. Task-board uses the\n9568|   source bundle and does not call the direct-provider fork operation.\n9569|5. Invoke tagged <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9570|   <code>intent=fork</code>, the fresh destination session as the sole\n9571|   materialization member, an empty ownership-transfer set, the source and\n9572|   derived workspace manifests, and the exact projection. A direct native fork\n9573|   uses <code>kind=workspace</code> and the destination group as the Plan\n9574|   subject; a supported provider import or task-board clone uses\n9575|   <code>kind=composite</code> and the destination session as subject. Invoke\n9576|   <code>materialize.commit</code> to install the new copy/worktree and any\n9577|   provider/task-board branch in rollbackable prepared state.\n9578|6. For a direct provider, execute only the already validated fork Spawn Plan\n9579|   through <code>ax pane NEW_SESSION_ID</code> with the new lease/profile. A\n9580|   native fork allocates its new handle at that start; a supported import uses\n9581|   the prepared provider store. Call <code>identify-session</code>, require a\n9582|   new identity unequal to the source and equal to any planned native ID,\n9583|   persist its Provider Identity Record, and validate native discovery. Then\n9584|   finalize with <code>direct_owner_resumed</code>, the derived profile, and\n9585|   null new-session profile source.\n9586|7. For task-board, commit performs journaled bundle import/open in\n9587|   <code>fork</code> mode and requires a new manager/provider identity and\n9588|   independent goal-binding state. Finalize with\n9589|   <code>task_board_owner_resumed</code> adopts/resumes under the new epoch-1\n9590|   binding and derived profile with null new-session profile source. No raw bridge operation occurs outside the\n9591|   materialization coordinator.\n9592|8. After successful finalize, record <code>fork.created</code> with the source\n9593|   provenance, new Session Record ID, effective profile,\n9594|   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>, the source checkpoint's nullable\n9595|   profile event in <code>source_profile_event_id</code>, and mode; then record\n9596|   <code>session.resumed</code> with the new-record profile and null source. A lost\n9597|   response is reconciled by materialization and provider/bridge status before\n9598|   either event is emitted exactly once.\n9599|\n9600|The exact Fork Provenance fixture for operation\n9601|<code>0198f4c8-28f0-7900-897a-1234567890ab</code> is:\n9602|\n9603|~~~json\n9604|{\n9605|  \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9606|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n9607|  \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9608|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-28f0-7900-897a-1234567890ab\",\n9609|  \"provider_fork_mode\": \"native\",\n9610|  \"extensions\": {}\n9611|}\n9612|~~~\n9613|\n9614|For <code>FORK-PROJECTION-POS</code>, the exact projection—and therefore the\n9615|complete inputs for deriving the newly persisted Workspace Group Record—is:\n9616|\n9617|~~~json\n9618|{\n9619|  \"projection_version\": \"workspace_fork_v1\",\n9620|  \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9621|  \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9622|  \"source_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n9623|  \"source_workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n9624|  \"destination_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9625|  \"destination_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9626|  \"destination_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:8f9fceda7f56a1e5c28c73192a915741c3b5fb6229e199b9b071b266136f7cf4\",\n9627|  \"destination_display_name\": \"payments-api-experiment\",\n9628|  \"destination_created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9629|  \"destination_created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:29:58.000Z\",\n9630|  \"destination_extensions\": {},\n9631|  \"member_mappings\": [\n9632|    {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"payments-api\"},\n9633|    {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"design-notes\"}\n9634|  ],\n9635|  \"manifest_mappings\": [\n9636|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:7cff7402aa5a31ba0cd7ff9bf49a9dc166b961c9f2b647d1c1084d3e70ce5db8\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:82864b91f66b77e032b5c9aeb86e20091bdf88f6d461e2a26e0d2f4107cfa306\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-3234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7de0-7e55-8e6f-4234567890ab\"},\n9637|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:88d93f20f978b92e75d35e67ebd5a41b90ff1afe106363b05c0f7b08614eb4cf\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:549245f73bff80001d7f2310b06c446124100028e5301083189460b8829a476c\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\"},\n9638|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:8dc15e881e026e7cf59482395baaa8c47341e6bad6d87f44312a9d0b360aacd5\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:dd2b8f604b2934127616623b7c70240a6c3acc8e6cdfe6ebdfbf137160abeaaf\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\"},\n9639|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_group\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\"}\n9640|  ]\n9641|}\n9642|~~~\n9643|\n9644|The following complete <code>FORK-PLAN-DIRECT-POS</code> object is the\n9645|workspace-only transaction for a provider-native fork. Its provider has no\n9646|portable-store mutation; the new native identity is created only by the\n9647|post-prepare Spawn Plan. The destination root is absent and configured as the\n9648|logical root <code>relux-forks</code>:\n9649|\n9650|~~~jsonc\n9651|{\n9652|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan\",\n9653|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n9654|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:d4365a3e3c8736704febcabd008e458c6c661c329df444c2b79439b2b6d41dbb\",\n9655|  \"kind\": \"workspace\",\n9656|  \"intent\": \"fork\",\n9657|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9658|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n9659|  \"source_manifest_ids\": [\"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\"],\n9660|  \"derived_manifest_ids\": [\n9661|    \"sha256:549245f73bff80001d7f2310b06c446124100028e5301083189460b8829a476c\",\n9662|    \"sha256:82864b91f66b77e032b5c9aeb86e20091bdf88f6d461e2a26e0d2f4107cfa306\",\n9663|    \"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\n9664|    \"sha256:dd2b8f604b2934127616623b7c70240a6c3acc8e6cdfe6ebdfbf137160abeaaf\"\n9665|  ],\n9666|  \"fork_projection\": {\n9667|    \"projection_version\": \"workspace_fork_v1\",\n9668|    \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9669|    \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9670|    \"source_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n9671|    \"source_workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n9672|    \"destination_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9673|    \"destination_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9674|    \"destination_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:8f9fceda7f56a1e5c28c73192a915741c3b5fb6229e199b9b071b266136f7cf4\",\n9675|    \"destination_display_name\": \"payments-api-experiment\",\n9676|    \"destination_created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9677|    \"destination_created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:29:58.000Z\",\n9678|    \"destination_extensions\": {},\n9679|    \"member_mappings\": [\n9680|      {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"payments-api\"},\n9681|      {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"design-notes\"}\n9682|    ],\n9683|    \"manifest_mappings\": [\n9684|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:7cff7402aa5a31ba0cd7ff9bf49a9dc166b961c9f2b647d1c1084d3e70ce5db8\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:82864b91f66b77e032b5c9aeb86e20091bdf88f6d461e2a26e0d2f4107cfa306\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-3234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7de0-7e55-8e6f-4234567890ab\"},\n9685|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:88d93f20f978b92e75d35e67ebd5a41b90ff1afe106363b05c0f7b08614eb4cf\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:549245f73bff80001d7f2310b06c446124100028e5301083189460b8829a476c\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\"},\n9686|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:8dc15e881e026e7cf59482395baaa8c47341e6bad6d87f44312a9d0b360aacd5\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:dd2b8f604b2934127616623b7c70240a6c3acc8e6cdfe6ebdfbf137160abeaaf\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\"},\n9687|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_group\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\"}\n9688|    ]\n9689|  },\n9690|  \"prepared_for_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9691|  \"source_lease_epoch\": 4,\n9692|  \"source_lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n9693|  \"authorities\": [\n9694|    {\"authority_id\":\"workspace_fork\",\"kind\":\"workspace\",\"platform\":\"linux\",\"root_path\":\"/srv/relux-forks\",\"logical_root\":\"relux-forks\",\"workspace_group_id\":\"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\"write_policy\":\"managed_copy\"}\n9695|  ],\n9696|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": null,\n9697|  \"operations\": [\n9698|    {\"sequence\":1,\"action\":\"install_workspace_group\",\"authority_id\":\"workspace_fork\",\"target_relative_path\":\"payments-api-experiment\",\"input_id\":\"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\"expected_prior_digest\":null,\"atomicity_boundary\":\"target_directory\"}\n9699|  ],\n9700|  \"exclusions\": [\"credential\",\"live_pid\",\"machine_auth\",\"socket\",\"transient_lock\"],\n9701|  \"validations\": [\"manifest_closure\",\"workspace_state\"],\n9702|  \"commit_strategy\": \"atomic_directory_rename\",\n9703|  \"rollback_required\": true,\n9704|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9705|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:29:59.000Z\",\n9706|  \"extensions\": {}\n9707|}\n9708|~~~\n9709|\n9710|The source manifest objects in Section 10.4 are the language-neutral input\n9711|bytes. Applying <code>workspace_fork_v1</code> MUST reproduce all four displayed\n9712|destination IDs: the submodule working tree, Git working tree, managed tree,\n9713|and group root in that order. Implementations MUST compare the fully derived\n9714|JCS bytes, not accept the mapping as an unchecked assertion.\n9715|\n9716|The transaction variants are exact:\n9717|\n9718|| Fixture | Prepare/commit input | Activation and terminal journal |\n9719|| --- | --- | --- |\n9720|| <code>FORK-TXN-DIRECT-NATIVE</code> | The displayed workspace plan, fresh session cohort, empty transfer set | Commit prepares the new workspace; the validated Spawn Plan creates one new native identity; finalize <code>direct_owner_resumed</code> commits the marker and leaves both provider/task-board transaction states <code>none</code> |\n9721|| <code>FORK-TXN-DIRECT-IMPORT</code> | Composite fork plan formed from the same projection plus the exact provider manifest/authority/operation returned for <code>mode=fork</code> | Commit leaves workspace and provider transaction prepared; discovery must find a new identity; finalize commits both only after process proof |\n9722|| <code>FORK-TXN-TASK-BOARD</code> | Composite fork plan formed from the same projection plus the source Task-board Bundle and one fresh task-board staging authority | Commit records import/open with <code>activation_mode=fork</code> and bridge <code>open mode=fork</code>; finalize adopts/resumes the new manager under the new lease, then commits marker and journal |\n9723|\n9724|“Formed from” is the Section 10.5 composite tagged-union operation: it copies\n9725|the displayed source/derived/projection facts and workspace\n9726|authority/operation, unions exactly one permitted provider or task-board\n9727|authority/operation set, sorts authorities/operations/validations, renumbers\n9728|operations consecutively, sets the Plan kind/subject to composite/destination\n9729|session, selects <code>two_phase_multi_root</code>, and recomputes its ID. It is\n9730|not an out-of-band second transaction. In all three rows, a failure before\n9731|activation rolls the one prepared materialization back; a failure after\n9732|process start or adopt is recovered by status/finalize or an explicit fenced\n9733|stop and never by restoring bytes behind a live owner.\n9734|\n9735|The fork Session Record MUST carry those values byte-for-byte for this fixture;\n9736|the <code>fork.created</code> event repeats source/checkpoint/record digest and\n9737|mode so a validator can join provenance without interpreting extensions.\n9738|\n9739|Normative fork Session Record using that provenance:\n9740|\n9741|~~~json\n9742|{\n9743|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n9744|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n9745|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:83c7152b9415c20c90e9009e1fe2e01f9cd3a45ca385b5bc2d678e979756427f\",\n9746|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9747|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9748|  \"name\": \"payments-api-experiment\",\n9749|  \"kind\": \"direct\",\n9750|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:30:00.000Z\",\n9751|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9752|  \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n9753|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9754|  \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n9755|  \"launch_plan\": {\n9756|    \"argv\": [\"codex\"],\n9757|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\",\n9758|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n9759|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n9760|    \"env_literals\": {},\n9761|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n9762|    \"extensions\": {}\n9763|  },\n9764|  \"task_board\": null,\n9765|  \"fork_provenance\": {\n9766|    \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9767|    \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n9768|    \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9769|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-28f0-7900-897a-1234567890ab\",\n9770|    \"provider_fork_mode\": \"native\",\n9771|    \"extensions\": {}\n9772|  },\n9773|  \"extensions\": {}\n9774|}\n9775|~~~\n9776|\n9777|The source lease, provider identity, history, and process are not changed.\n9778|Muse forks with non-empty or active <code>cron.db</code> are unsupported because\n9779|scheduled work could duplicate. Antigravity fork requires the authenticated\n9780|backend's native fork surface; copying local cache/transcripts is not a fork.\n9781|When a provider cannot fork faithfully, the command MUST report\n9782|<code>provider_fork_unsupported</code>; it MUST NOT relabel a blank chat as a\n9783|fork.\n9784|\n9785|Fork failure and recovery are exact:\n9786|\n9787|| Fixture/boundary | Required result |\n9788|| --- | --- |\n9789|| <code>FORK-BEFORE-TOPOLOGY</code> | Validation/allocation failure writes no destination topology, Session Record, lease, provider, or manager |\n9790|| <code>FORK-AFTER-TOPOLOGY</code> | Derived topology/manifests exist but Session Record does not; they remain harmless unreferenced immutable objects eligible for ordinary GC |\n9791|| <code>FORK-AFTER-SESSION</code> | New Session Record and epoch-1 lease exist, but no materialization; state is <code>creating</code> and the same operation may resume at prepare |\n9792|| <code>FORK-MATERIALIZE-NEG</code> | Prepare/commit fails before activation; rollback restores destination, new fork remains failed/creating owner, source is untouched |\n9793|| <code>FORK-DIRECT-IDENTITY-NEG</code> | Provider fork cannot prove a new identity; roll back pre-activation transaction and report <code>provider_fork_unsupported</code>; never use the source or a blank identity |\n9794|| <code>FORK-TB-OPEN-NEG</code> | Import/open fails; journal/status/expiry recovery applies and no manager is adopted |\n9795|| <code>FORK-AFTER-ACTIVATION</code> | Provider/manager is running but finalize response is lost; reconcile status and finalize with the same IDs; byte rollback or a second process is forbidden |\n9796|| <code>FORK-EVENT-LOST</code> | Finalize committed but event publication failed; retry the same event identities and do not recreate topology, lease, provider, or manager |\n9797|\n9798|No fork failure changes the source lease, event chain, provider identity,\n9799|manager binding, workspace marker, or checkpoint. A fork with an authoritative\n9800|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> is non-resumable and remains failed.\n9801|\n9802|### 13.9 Stop\n9803|\n9804|<code>ax stop NAME</code> is graceful by default and executes on the current\n9805|owner, locally or through authenticated <code>session.stop</code> RPC.\n9806|\n9807|Preconditions are a winning owner lease and an available quiesce/stop path.\n9808|Transitions:\n9809|\n9810|1. block input and enter <code>quiescing</code>;\n9811|2. wait for a complete safe boundary;\n9812|3. create and sync a validated checkpoint;\n9813|4. request normal provider/task-board stop;\n9814|5. require process exit and closed durable handles;\n9815|6. if normal exit appended provider/manager closure records, capture and sync a\n9816|   closure-only delta and superseding validated checkpoint; an unexpected\n9817|   workspace/background mutation fails closed while ownership remains local;\n9818|7. record and sync <code>session.stopped</code> with the newest checkpoint; and\n9819|8. retain the same lease, native store, workspace, terminal metadata, and\n9820|   checkpoints.\n9821|\n9822|For a task-board session, steps 1–3 use bridge\n9823|<code>export --mode handoff</code>, step 4 consumes its source-control token\n9824|with bridge <code>stop</code>, and any replacement closure bundle returned in\n9825|step 6 remains opaque. For a direct session, the equivalent actions use the\n9826|provider plugin and terminal backend.\n9827|\n9828|A graceful timeout leaves ownership unchanged and reports\n9829|<code>quiesce_timeout</code> or <code>stop_timeout</code>. The process MAY be\n9830|unquiesced if safe. <code>ax stop NAME --force</code> requires explicit\n9831|confirmation, preserves best-effort diagnostics/checkpoint state, terminates\n9832|the local process, records unclean stop, and does not imply a safe transferable\n9833|checkpoint.\n9834|\n9835|The ordinary successful path returns a non-null final checkpoint,\n9836|<code>resumable=true</code>, <code>bootstrap_aborted=false</code>, and state\n9837|<code>stopped</code>. If the epoch-1 lease has no checkpoint, graceful stop MUST\n9838|either establish the first validated checkpoint and take that ordinary path or\n9839|fail without publishing a stop event. Confirmed force closure in that bootstrap\n9840|window returns a null checkpoint, <code>resumable=false</code>,\n9841|<code>bootstrap_aborted=true</code>, and state <code>failed</code>, after\n9842|publishing the exact two events in Section 13.1. A force stop of a session that\n9843|already has a checkpoint keeps that checkpoint ID, is resumable only from that\n9844|older checkpoint, sets <code>bootstrap_aborted=false</code>, and returns\n9845|<code>stopped</code> only after process/store closure is proved. An unknown\n9846|process or open store handle returns failure and leaves the command retryable;\n9847|it is never represented as a successful closure.\n9848|\n9849|Stop is not delete. Deletion requires a separate future/administrative surface\n9850|that emits a Session Tombstone; v0.3.0 MUST NOT make stop delete state.\n9851|\n9852|### 13.10 Resume\n9853|\n9854|<code>ax resume NAME</code> is allowed only on the winning owner host. A replica\n9855|receives <code>not_owner</code> and explicit attach/takeover/fork choices.\n9856|\n9857|The owner first refreshes lease knowledge and verifies its fencing token. If\n9858|the epoch-1 winning lease has a null checkpoint, resume is not an ordinary\n9859|resume: it executes only the Section 13.1/13.2 bootstrap retry predicate and\n9860|phase continuation. An authoritative bootstrap-abort event returns\n9861|<code>checkpoint_unavailable</code> and cannot be resumed. No later epoch may\n9862|have a null checkpoint.\n9863|\n9864|For a validated checkpoint, derive the exact effective profile/source from its\n9865|event-head closure, probe the mapping/capabilities, and choose exactly one path:\n9866|\n9867|1. <strong>No materialization.</strong> If the current managed marker and native\n9868|   provider/bridge status already equal the checkpoint and winning lease, do\n9869|   not create a transaction. Direct sessions validate native discovery, start\n9870|   <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>, invoke plugin resume with the effective\n9871|   profile, prove the process, and emit <code>session.resumed</code>. A\n9872|   task-board session validates the existing manager binding and calls the\n9873|   public bridge resume with a caller-stable ID/profile, proves status, and\n9874|   emits the event. A missing binding does not qualify for this path.\n9875|2. <strong>Direct materialization.</strong> Call tagged\n9876|   <code>materialize.prepare</code> with <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, the\n9877|   owner as the sole materialization member, empty ownership-transfer set, and\n9878|   workspace/provider/composite kind. Call commit and require durable\n9879|   <code>prepared</code>. Validate native discovery or exact backend identity,\n9880|   start the wrapper, invoke plugin resume, and prove the exact session. Then\n9881|   finalize with <code>direct_owner_resumed</code> and the effective\n9882|   profile/source; only a committed result permits <code>session.resumed</code>.\n9883|3. <strong>Task-board materialization.</strong> Prepare with task-board or\n9884|   composite kind and the same cohort rules. Commit installs the opaque bundle,\n9885|   imports, and opens dormant through the journal. Finalize with\n9886|   <code>task_board_owner_resumed</code>, the winning binding, and effective\n9887|   profile/source; finalize adopts/resumes and proves public bridge status.\n9888|   Only its committed result permits adoption/resume events.\n9889|\n9890|Every materializing path is therefore\n9891|prepare → commit/prepared → identity or dormant validation → activation →\n9892|finalize/committed. A response lost at any arrow is recovered with\n9893|<code>materialize.status</code> plus plugin/bridge status under the same IDs.\n9894|Before direct process start or task-board adopt, validation failure, operator\n9895|abort, or lease loss invokes rollback. After a direct process is proven running\n9896|or task-board adopt succeeds, ordinary byte rollback is forbidden: the same\n9897|owner must finish status/finalize, stop the activation, or perform a new fenced\n9898|ownership operation. Failure leaves the session stopped/failed on that same\n9899|owner and preserves the journal.\n9900|\n9901|Normative resume fixtures are:\n9902|\n9903|| Fixture | Kind/path | Required terminal result |\n9904|| --- | --- | --- |\n9905|| <code>RESUME-NO-MAT-DIRECT</code> | Current workspace/native identity; no transaction | Same lease/profile, exact provider resumed, one resumed event |\n9906|| <code>RESUME-WORKSPACE</code> | Workspace-only prepare/commit, direct native state already current | Marker committed after direct activation; provider transaction remains none |\n9907|| <code>RESUME-PROVIDER</code> | Provider-only prepared transaction | Null marker/path; provider transaction commits only after exact resume |\n9908|| <code>RESUME-COMPOSITE-DIRECT</code> | Workspace plus portable provider | Both roots prepared; exact provider running before finalize cleans backups |\n9909|| <code>RESUME-TASK-BOARD</code> | Task-board-only bundle | Journal opened → adopted → resumed; null marker/path |\n9910|| <code>RESUME-COMPOSITE-TB</code> | Workspace plus bundle | Workspace remains rollbackable until bridge resume proof; then marker/finalize |\n9911|| <code>RESUME-PRE-ACTIVATION-NEG</code> | Any prepared path fails validation | Roll back and remain stopped owner |\n9912|| <code>RESUME-POST-ACTIVATION-NEG</code> | Activation succeeds, response/finalize fails | Status-recover/finalize or explicitly stop; never roll back behind live activation |\n9913|\n9914|It MUST not create a new native session under the old logical identity.\n9915|Antigravity backend <code>not found</code> is\n9916|<code>unsupported_backend_identity</code>, not a successful blank resume.\n9917|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5fb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":344,"recorded_at":1780531400000683,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0add0-7f3b-78a1-9d35-1235392038e2"},"task_id":"01a0add0-7f3b-78a1-9d35-1235392038e2","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0add0-7f3b-78a1-9d35-1235392038e2"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5fd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":345,"recorded_at":1780531400000685,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"call_id":"call_01a0add07ab675a1949c498e37159d50","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(9252 line(s) above)\n9253|### 13.6 Graceful takeover\n9254|\n9255|Command form is <code>ax takeover NAME --to HOST</code>; <code>--to</code>\n9256|defaults to the local host in interactive use.\n9257|\n9258|Preconditions:\n9259|\n9260|- source is reachable and proves it holds the winning lease;\n9261|- destination is allowlisted, is not the source, and has compatible contracts;\n9262|- destination provider/platform capabilities required by the session are\n9263|  available;\n9264|- on macOS, the destination Aqua broker, dedicated AX tmux server generation,\n9265|  functional sentinel, and separate provider-auth smoke are current for the\n9266|  selected provider build and macOS version;\n9267|- workspace-group members can all be quiesced or separated into worktrees;\n9268|- one exact WorkspaceGroupExpectation and Section 12.6 workspace mode have\n9269|  been selected;\n9270|- destination conflicts are absent or already resolved;\n9271|- task-board bridge is available for a task-board session; and\n9272|- no other takeover operation is active for the session.\n9273|\n9274|Transitions:\n9275|\n9276|1. Destination allocates one group operation ID and one session operation ID\n9277|   for each migration-cohort member. It calls <code>handoff.prepare</code> for\n9278|   each, naming the identical WorkspaceGroupExpectation, source lease,\n9279|   destination host, expected source checkpoint, and MaterializationCohort whose\n9280|   two arrays both equal the selected migration cohort. A single-member cohort\n9281|   still carries the exact expectation and one-element arrays.\n9282|2. Source blocks new input and changes <code>running|idle</code> to\n9283|   <code>quiescing</code>.\n9284|3. Through <code>handoff.quiesce</code>, source calls provider or task-board\n9285|   quiesce and waits for a complete safe boundary. A task-board source uses\n9286|   bridge <code>export --mode handoff</code>, requires\n9287|   <code>BridgeSafeBoundary.safe = true</code>, maps it exactly to RPC and\n9288|   checkpoint evidence, and retains its source-control token. Timeout or an\n9289|   incomplete bridge proof fails closed.\n9290|4. Source captures a fresh checkpoint under the current lease. A direct source\n9291|   uses the Section 7.5 Object Sink path for a portable provider snapshot or a\n9292|   validated zero-entry identity manifest for a backend-only provider; a\n9293|   task-board source uses only the opaque bundle. Both use the exact Section\n9294|   10.4 workspace-group root.\n9295|5. Source performs the final bulk record/blob/workspace/board sync to\n9296|   destination.\n9297|6. Destination stages, validates, and conflict-checks every referenced object.\n9298|   It does not resume. Destination broker and provider-auth readiness MUST be\n9299|   proved before ownership commit; a diagnostic Aqua manager name or sentinel\n9300|   alone is not proof.\n9301|7. Destination calls <code>handoff.stop</code>. Source requests graceful\n9302|   provider/task-board stop, verifies process exit and durable-store closure,\n9303|   and records <code>session.stopped</code>. A task-board source consumes the\n9304|   bridge source-control token with bridge <code>stop</code>.\n9305|8. If normal exit appended provider/manager closure records, source captures a\n9306|   closure-only delta, creates a superseding validated checkpoint, and syncs\n9307|   that delta. Any unexpected workspace/background mutation fails the graceful\n9308|   flow while the source remains the stopped owner.\n9309|9. Destination calls tagged <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9310|   <code>intent = ownership_transfer</code>, the exact non-empty selected cohort\n9311|   in both cohort arrays, and kind workspace/provider/task-board/composite from\n9312|   the checkpoint sources. It then performs atomic materialization through RPC\n9313|   <code>materialize.commit</code>, which leaves a durable rollbackable prepared\n9314|   transaction; a direct portable-store path invokes provider\n9315|   <code>materialize</code> inside it. For task-board, destination also performs\n9316|   the journaled Section 10.6 import/open sequence inside commit, never before\n9317|   prepare. No prepared path accepts input.\n9318|10. After every migration-cohort member is stopped/prepared and group\n9319|   expectation still matches, destination creates each member's epoch\n9320|   <code>source_epoch + 1</code>, predecessor source\n9321|   lease, reason <code>graceful_takeover</code>, and checkpoint from step 4.\n9322|   When step 8 created a superseding checkpoint, that checkpoint replaces the\n9323|   step-4 checkpoint in this lease.\n9324|   Destination persists each lease, then calls <code>handoff.commit</code> so source and\n9325|   destination union and persist that Lease Record. Destination MUST verify it\n9326|   is still the winning lease after union; if a concurrent higher/winning lease\n9327|   exists, it MUST NOT adopt or resume.\n9328|11. For a direct session, destination validates native discovery and resumes\n9329|    through <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> with the checkpoint-derived\n9330|    effective profile and new fencing token, using plugin <code>resume</code>.\n9331|    For task-board, destination performs no out-of-band adopt or resume.\n9332|12. After exact direct process status proves the owner resumed, destination\n9333|    invokes <code>materialize.finalize</code> with\n9334|    <code>direct_owner_resumed</code>, the effective profile, and its source\n9335|    event. For task-board, it invokes finalize with\n9336|    <code>task_board_owner_resumed</code>; finalize consumes the journaled open\n9337|    token, adopts the exact binding, resumes with that profile, and proves\n9338|    bridge status. Finalize commits any provider transaction and removes\n9339|    rollback bytes. A lost response is recovered with\n9340|    <code>materialize.status</code>.\n9341|13. Source becomes a replica, its wrapper parks, and destination publishes\n9342|    <code>lease.transferred</code> and <code>session.resumed</code> for every\n9343|    moved member. The resumed event repeats the exact effective profile/source\n9344|    used by finalize. Whole-group mode reports all affected session IDs; separate-\n9345|    worktrees mode reports only the selected session.\n9346|\n9347|Failure and recovery are phase-specific:\n9348|\n9349|| Failure boundary | Authority | Required recovery |\n9350|| --- | --- | --- |\n9351|| Before source stop | Source lease remains owner and process MAY be unquiesced; destination staging is inert | Abort handoff, resume source input, or retry same operation |\n9352|| After source stop, before destination lease | Source remains logical owner but is stopped; destination is a replica | Retry materialization, resume source, or restart takeover from the same checkpoint |\n9353|| After destination lease is persisted | Destination is owner; source MUST NOT resume | Retry destination adopt/resume; a failed pre-resume prepared transaction may roll back destination bytes while authority stays at destination; if activation remains impossible, gracefully transfer back from stopped state or perform explicit force recovery |\n9354|| After provider resume/finalize but before response | Destination lease plus provider and materialization status decide success, not the lost client response | Retry operation ID; inspect provider/bridge and <code>materialize.status</code>; do not create another epoch or guess rollback |\n9355|\n9356|No failure before step 10 MAY advance ownership. No failure after step 10 MAY\n9357|allow the old source to resume.\n9358|Before step 10, abort recovery MUST use <code>handoff.abort</code> so the source\n9359|records whether it unquiesced or remained stopped. After step 10,\n9360|<code>handoff.abort</code> MUST refuse because ownership recovery requires a new\n9361|lease transition.\n9362|\n9363|### 13.7 Force takeover\n9364|\n9365|Force takeover is an explicit recovery operation:\n9366|\n9367|~~~shell\n9368|ax takeover NAME --to HOST --force --expect-owner HOST_ID --expect-epoch EPOCH\n9369|~~~\n9370|\n9371|Interactive use MUST display that the old process can still exist, split-brain\n9372|history can result, and both histories will be preserved. Non-interactive use\n9373|MUST include destination, both expected values, and <code>--yes</code>.\n9374|\n9375|Force takeover MUST NOT claim or require a verified source-process stop. It is\n9376|the explicit exception to the graceful stop-before-commit sequence because the\n9377|source may be unreachable and its old process may still exist. Destination\n9378|realm and provider-auth readiness MUST be proved before the force lease is\n9379|persisted. Only the winning committed force lease authorizes destination\n9380|runtime creation; its fencing token rejects the prior owner from authoritative\n9381|sync or resume, and the old process MAY continue until it observes that losing\n9382|lease and parks or stops. This exception does not weaken the readiness-before-\n9383|ownership or runtime-after-ownership requirements.\n9384|\n9385|Preconditions:\n9386|\n9387|- destination is allowlisted and not known to hold a losing lease;\n9388|- the operator supplies/accepts the observed owner and epoch;\n9389|- the newest available checkpoint is integrity-valid; and\n9390|- destination materialization is either conflict-free or explicitly directed\n9391|  to a new copy/worktree;\n9392|- one exact WorkspaceGroupExpectation and Section 12.6 workspace mode are\n9393|  selected; whole-group mode has a recovery checkpoint for every migration\n9394|  member;\n9395|- the complete Session Record, provider identity, and persisted profile are\n9396|  available; and\n9397|- no local process is using the proposed destination native-store/workspace\n9398|  paths.\n9399|\n9400|A direct session additionally requires an accepted <code>native_resume</code>\n9401|tuple and one of two exact recovery bases: an accepted\n9402|<code>portable_store</code> plan, or a provider probe proving that the\n9403|destination's machine-local authenticated backend already resolves the exact\n9404|Provider Identity Record without copied store bytes. Required destination\n9405|credentials remain machine-local. The terminal backend and profile mapping\n9406|MUST pass before lease advance.\n9407|\n9408|A task-board session additionally requires bridge protocol 1.0.0 with\n9409|status/import/open/adopt/resume, an integrity-valid opaque bundle from the\n9410|selected checkpoint, and destination-local board/provider authentication. A\n9411|local board requires its staged <code>.task-board</code> tree and a successful\n9412|standalone <code>task-board validate</code>; a remote board requires access to\n9413|the exact logical board identity. <code>ax</code> MUST NOT substitute a whole-\n9414|board archive or inspect private manager state.\n9415|\n9416|Common pre-lease preparation and fencing are:\n9417|\n9418|1. Allocate one group operation and one takeover <code>operation_id</code> per\n9419|   migration member; attempt best-effort lease refresh and sync. Lack of source\n9420|   contact is not fatal. Every member uses the same WorkspaceGroupExpectation\n9421|   and MaterializationCohort with both arrays equal to the selected recovery\n9422|   cohort.\n9423|2. Preserve local destination divergence as an independent checkpoint or\n9424|   select a new copy/worktree. Select one immutable source checkpoint and pin\n9425|   all referenced object IDs.\n9426|3. Stage and validate workspace state without mutating the destination. For a\n9427|   direct session, also stage the accepted provider plan or prove exact backend\n9428|   identity resolution. For task-board, validate the opaque bundle and bridge\n9429|   capability/authentication only; bridge import/open is forbidden until\n9430|   <code>materialize.prepare</code> has durably created the transaction journal\n9431|   and fresh staging authority. No pre-lease staging accepts input.\n9432|4. Re-run membership, conflict, disk, terminal, provider/bridge,\n9433|   authentication, and profile\n9434|   checks. Any failure through this step aborts with the observed lease still\n9435|   authoritative. Staging and dormant state remain inert and may be retried or\n9436|   garbage-collected by their token-expiry rules.\n9437|5. Display/require the split-brain confirmation. Persist a machine-local\n9438|   confirmation receipt bound to operation ID, expected owner/epoch,\n9439|   checkpoint, destination, and all three accepted risks.\n9440|6. In whole-group mode, require all member confirmations and validated inert\n9441|   object staging before selecting each <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code>.\n9442|   Provider and task-board materialization journals do not yet exist. Create a\n9443|   new random lease ID with reason <code>force_takeover</code> and that member's\n9444|   selected checkpoint, and durably persist it. In separate-worktrees mode this\n9445|   applies only to the selected session. Ownership MUST NOT advance before\n9446|   steps 1–5 pass for the full selected cohort.\n9447|7. Recompute the winner after every reachable peer response. If this lease has\n9448|   already lost, do not materialize, adopt, or resume. If it wins, emit\n9449|   <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> followed by\n9450|   <code>lease.forced</code> under the new lease; the former must exactly match\n9451|   the receipt and accepted-risk tuple in Section 5.2.\n9452|\n9453|The direct path then MUST:\n9454|\n9455|1. invoke tagged RPC <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9456|   <code>intent = ownership_transfer</code>, the exact selected non-empty cohort,\n9457|   and provider/composite kind as workspace participation requires, then invoke\n9458|   <code>materialize.commit</code> to enter a rollbackable prepared\n9459|   workspace transaction and, only when <code>portable_store</code> is\n9460|   available, invoke plugin <code>materialize</code> inside it with the new\n9461|   fencing token;\n9462|2. validate native discovery of the exact Provider Identity Record, or validate\n9463|   exact authenticated-backend resolution for a backend-only identity;\n9464|3. fail with <code>unsupported_backend_identity</code> or\n9465|   <code>native_store_conflict</code> rather than create or relabel a blank\n9466|   provider session; and\n9467|4. call plugin <code>resume</code>, launch the returned plan through\n9468|   <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>, revalidate the lease before input, and\n9469|   prove the process is the exact native session; and\n9470|5. invoke RPC <code>materialize.finalize</code> with\n9471|   <code>activation = direct_owner_resumed</code>, the checkpoint-derived\n9472|   effective profile/source, recover a lost response through\n9473|   status, and only then publish <code>session.resumed</code>.\n9474|\n9475|The task-board path then MUST:\n9476|\n9477|1. invoke tagged RPC <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9478|   <code>intent = ownership_transfer</code>, the exact selected non-empty cohort,\n9479|   and task-board/composite kind as workspace participation requires, then enter\n9480|   a rollbackable prepared transaction. Commit performs the exact journaled\n9481|   bundle installation, bridge import, and dormant open; for a local board, run\n9482|   standalone <code>task-board validate</code> again against prepared bytes;\n9483|2. call <code>materialize.finalize</code> with\n9484|   <code>activation = task_board_owner_resumed</code>, the exact new binding,\n9485|   and checkpoint-derived effective profile/source. The coordinator consumes\n9486|   its journaled open token, adopts, verifies status, resumes, verifies status,\n9487|   and commits transaction cleanup;\n9488|3. publish <code>task_board.adopted</code> and\n9489|   <code>session.resumed</code> from the recovered finalize result, exactly\n9490|   once and with the same effective profile/source; and\n9491|4. never access the manager record, provider snapshot, or goal binding except\n9492|   as opaque bridge/bundle data.\n9493|\n9494|On later union, all peers apply the deterministic lease rule. The prior owner\n9495|becomes stale, while losing-lease events and checkpoints remain in divergent-\n9496|history branches for reconciliation.\n9497|\n9498|Failure and recovery are path- and phase-specific:\n9499|\n9500|| Boundary | Authority and required recovery |\n9501|| --- | --- |\n9502|| Any direct capability, identity, store-plan, or staging failure before step 6 | No new lease exists. Abort safely, retain resumable staging when useful, and leave the observed owner unchanged. |\n9503|| Any task-board authentication, bundle, or board-validation failure before step 6 | No new lease exists and no bridge import/open has occurred. Discard inert staging or retry from the immutable bundle. No blank manager/provider session may be opened. |\n9504|| New force lease loses before activation | The deterministic winner owns. Roll back every prepared host/provider transaction, leave task-board state dormant, and park this destination. |\n9505|| Direct materialization/native-discovery failure after step 6 | Destination remains the stopped or failed owner. Use RPC rollback, which consumes the provider rollback token internally, retain staging/history, and retry the same operation or perform a newer explicit takeover. Never roll ownership back. |\n9506|| Task-board commit/import/open fails after step 6 | Destination remains the stopped owner. Recover the journal with status or roll back pre-adopt bytes; a new prepare may allocate fresh bridge sub-operation IDs only after the prior transaction is terminal. |\n9507|| Task-board open token expires after step 6 but before adopt | Destination remains the stopped owner. Roll back the terminal pre-adopt transaction, then prepare/import/open the same immutable bundle in a new materialization; never reuse the staging root or mutate the old journal. |\n9508|| Task-board adopt returns no response | Recover <code>materialize.status</code>, which reconciles bridge status. Exact binding continues; no binding retries the same adopt ID while its token is valid; another binding is <code>lease_conflict</code>. Never inspect private state or guess. |\n9509|| Task-board adopt succeeds but resume fails | Destination is the adopted, stopped/failed owner. Retry finalize/bridge resume with the same persisted IDs; do not roll back bytes, unadopt, restore the old owner, or replace it with a blank provider session. |\n9510|| Provider/bridge or materialization finalization response is lost | Lease, terminal/bridge status, provider transaction status, and RPC <code>materialize.status</code> decide the result. Retry by operation ID and do not create another epoch or guess rollback. |\n9511|\n9512|The following sequence fixtures are normative. They start with source A at\n9513|epoch 4, destination B as replica, and checkpoint C4 unless a row says the\n9514|pre-lease gate fails:\n9515|\n9516|| Fixture | Required phase trace | Required terminal authority/state |\n9517|| --- | --- | --- |\n9518|| <code>FT-DIRECT-POS</code> | stage workspace/store or backend proof → validate identity/profile → confirm → persist B epoch 5 → prepare → commit/prepared → discover exact native identity → resume → finalize/committed | B epoch 5 running; A stale after convergence; force-confirmed and lease-forced events precede resumed |\n9519|| <code>FT-DIRECT-PRE-NEG</code> | direct capability or backend identity check fails before confirmation/fencing | A epoch 4 unchanged; B has inert staging only; no force audit event or epoch-5 lease |\n9520|| <code>FT-DIRECT-POST-NEG</code> | persist B epoch 5 → prepared materialization/native discovery fails → provider then host rollback | B epoch 5 stopped/failed; A stale after convergence; no resumed event and no blank native session |\n9521|| <code>FT-TB-POS</code> | validate bundle/auth → confirm → persist B epoch 5 → prepare journal/fresh root → commit/import/open dormant → finalize/adopt/resume | B epoch 5 running and adopted; A stale; adoption event precedes resumed |\n9522|| <code>FT-TB-AUTH-NEG</code> | destination board/provider authentication fails before import/open | A epoch 4 unchanged; no manager activation, force event, or epoch-5 lease |\n9523|| <code>FT-TB-TOKEN-NEG</code> | persist B epoch 5 → commit/import/open dormant → token expires before adopt | B epoch 5 stopped; roll back pre-adopt transaction, then prepare/re-import/re-open same bundle; authority never rolls back |\n9524|| <code>FT-TB-ADOPT-UNKNOWN</code> | adopt response is lost → status returns exact binding, null, or different binding | Exact continues to resume; null retries dormant adopt; different fails lease conflict; B remains owner after epoch 5 |\n9525|| <code>FT-TB-RESUME-NEG</code> | adopt exact binding → bridge resume fails | B epoch 5 adopted and stopped/failed; retry resume only; no unadopt, A resume, or blank substitution |\n9526|\n9527|If two force takeovers choose the same epoch, bytewise greater lease ID wins.\n9528|The loser MUST stop accepting input when it learns the winner. If destination\n9529|cannot resume after acquiring the lease, it remains the stopped/failed owner;\n9530|recovery is retry, graceful transfer from stopped state, or a newer explicit\n9531|force takeover. Ownership MUST NOT roll back implicitly.\n9532|\n9533|### 13.8 Fork\n9534|\n9535|<code>ax fork NAME --from CHECKPOINT --as NEW_NAME [--to HOST]</code> defaults\n9536|to the newest validated checkpoint; destination defaults to local only in\n9537|interactive use. Non-interactive use MUST supply <code>--to</code>.\n9538|\n9539|Preconditions:\n9540|\n9541|- checkpoint and all referenced objects are available and valid;\n9542|- NEW_NAME is unused;\n9543|- destination workspace conflict policy is satisfied;\n9544|- provider <code>fork</code> can produce a new native identity or a sanitized\n9545|  new-session plan; and\n9546|- task-board supports bundle open in <code>fork</code> mode when applicable.\n9547|\n9548|Transitions:\n9549|\n9550|1. Allocate a caller-stable fork operation ID, a new logical session ID, a new\n9551|   workspace-group ID, a fresh workspace ID for every source topology member,\n9552|   and an epoch-1 lease owned by the destination. No source ID is reused.\n9553|2. Derive and validate the exact Section 10.5 ForkWorkspaceProjection. Persist\n9554|   the complete new Workspace Group Record and every re-identified destination\n9555|   Transfer Manifest before publishing any object that refers to them. Source\n9556|   topology/manifests remain byte-identical.\n9557|3. Derive the effective execution profile and nullable profile-source event\n9558|   from the selected source checkpoint. Create the new Session Record with that\n9559|   profile, the new group/member IDs, and required core\n9560|   <code>fork_provenance</code>; persist it and its epoch-1 lease. A failure\n9561|   before this point leaves only unreferenced immutable projection objects and\n9562|   no logical fork.\n9563|4. For a direct session, invoke the side-effect-free provider <code>fork</code>\n9564|   planning operation with the fork operation ID. For\n9565|   <code>supported_import</code>, call <code>native-store-plan</code> in\n9566|   <code>mode=fork</code> before prepare and validate its provider component;\n9567|   <code>native_fork</code> has no provider-store component. Task-board uses the\n9568|   source bundle and does not call the direct-provider fork operation.\n9569|5. Invoke tagged <code>materialize.prepare</code> with\n9570|   <code>intent=fork</code>, the fresh destination session as the sole\n9571|   materialization member, an empty ownership-transfer set, the source and\n9572|   derived workspace manifests, and the exact projection. A direct native fork\n9573|   uses <code>kind=workspace</code> and the destination group as the Plan\n9574|   subject; a supported provider import or task-board clone uses\n9575|   <code>kind=composite</code> and the destination session as subject. Invoke\n9576|   <code>materialize.commit</code> to install the new copy/worktree and any\n9577|   provider/task-board branch in rollbackable prepared state.\n9578|6. For a direct provider, execute only the already validated fork Spawn Plan\n9579|   through <code>ax pane NEW_SESSION_ID</code> with the new lease/profile. A\n9580|   native fork allocates its new handle at that start; a supported import uses\n9581|   the prepared provider store. Call <code>identify-session</code>, require a\n9582|   new identity unequal to the source and equal to any planned native ID,\n9583|   persist its Provider Identity Record, and validate native discovery. Then\n9584|   finalize with <code>direct_owner_resumed</code>, the derived profile, and\n9585|   null new-session profile source.\n9586|7. For task-board, commit performs journaled bundle import/open in\n9587|   <code>fork</code> mode and requires a new manager/provider identity and\n9588|   independent goal-binding state. Finalize with\n9589|   <code>task_board_owner_resumed</code> adopts/resumes under the new epoch-1\n9590|   binding and derived profile with null new-session profile source. No raw bridge operation occurs outside the\n9591|   materialization coordinator.\n9592|8. After successful finalize, record <code>fork.created</code> with the source\n9593|   provenance, new Session Record ID, effective profile,\n9594|   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>, the source checkpoint's nullable\n9595|   profile event in <code>source_profile_event_id</code>, and mode; then record\n9596|   <code>session.resumed</code> with the new-record profile and null source. A lost\n9597|   response is reconciled by materialization and provider/bridge status before\n9598|   either event is emitted exactly once.\n9599|\n9600|The exact Fork Provenance fixture for operation\n9601|<code>0198f4c8-28f0-7900-897a-1234567890ab</code> is:\n9602|\n9603|~~~json\n9604|{\n9605|  \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9606|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n9607|  \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9608|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-28f0-7900-897a-1234567890ab\",\n9609|  \"provider_fork_mode\": \"native\",\n9610|  \"extensions\": {}\n9611|}\n9612|~~~\n9613|\n9614|For <code>FORK-PROJECTION-POS</code>, the exact projection—and therefore the\n9615|complete inputs for deriving the newly persisted Workspace Group Record—is:\n9616|\n9617|~~~json\n9618|{\n9619|  \"projection_version\": \"workspace_fork_v1\",\n9620|  \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9621|  \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9622|  \"source_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n9623|  \"source_workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n9624|  \"destination_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9625|  \"destination_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9626|  \"destination_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:8f9fceda7f56a1e5c28c73192a915741c3b5fb6229e199b9b071b266136f7cf4\",\n9627|  \"destination_display_name\": \"payments-api-experiment\",\n9628|  \"destination_created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9629|  \"destination_created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:29:58.000Z\",\n9630|  \"destination_extensions\": {},\n9631|  \"member_mappings\": [\n9632|    {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"payments-api\"},\n9633|    {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"design-notes\"}\n9634|  ],\n9635|  \"manifest_mappings\": [\n9636|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:7cff7402aa5a31ba0cd7ff9bf49a9dc166b961c9f2b647d1c1084d3e70ce5db8\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:82864b91f66b77e032b5c9aeb86e20091bdf88f6d461e2a26e0d2f4107cfa306\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-3234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7de0-7e55-8e6f-4234567890ab\"},\n9637|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:88d93f20f978b92e75d35e67ebd5a41b90ff1afe106363b05c0f7b08614eb4cf\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:549245f73bff80001d7f2310b06c446124100028e5301083189460b8829a476c\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\"},\n9638|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:8dc15e881e026e7cf59482395baaa8c47341e6bad6d87f44312a9d0b360aacd5\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:dd2b8f604b2934127616623b7c70240a6c3acc8e6cdfe6ebdfbf137160abeaaf\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\"},\n9639|    {\"kind\":\"workspace_group\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\"}\n9640|  ]\n9641|}\n9642|~~~\n9643|\n9644|The following complete <code>FORK-PLAN-DIRECT-POS</code> object is the\n9645|workspace-only transaction for a provider-native fork. Its provider has no\n9646|portable-store mutation; the new native identity is created only by the\n9647|post-prepare Spawn Plan. The destination root is absent and configured as the\n9648|logical root <code>relux-forks</code>:\n9649|\n9650|~~~jsonc\n9651|{\n9652|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan\",\n9653|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n9654|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:d4365a3e3c8736704febcabd008e458c6c661c329df444c2b79439b2b6d41dbb\",\n9655|  \"kind\": \"workspace\",\n9656|  \"intent\": \"fork\",\n9657|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9658|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n9659|  \"source_manifest_ids\": [\"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\"],\n9660|  \"derived_manifest_ids\": [\n9661|    \"sha256:549245f73bff80001d7f2310b06c446124100028e5301083189460b8829a476c\",\n9662|    \"sha256:82864b91f66b77e032b5c9aeb86e20091bdf88f6d461e2a26e0d2f4107cfa306\",\n9663|    \"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\n9664|    \"sha256:dd2b8f604b2934127616623b7c70240a6c3acc8e6cdfe6ebdfbf137160abeaaf\"\n9665|  ],\n9666|  \"fork_projection\": {\n9667|    \"projection_version\": \"workspace_fork_v1\",\n9668|    \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9669|    \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9670|    \"source_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n9671|    \"source_workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n9672|    \"destination_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9673|    \"destination_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9674|    \"destination_workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:8f9fceda7f56a1e5c28c73192a915741c3b5fb6229e199b9b071b266136f7cf4\",\n9675|    \"destination_display_name\": \"payments-api-experiment\",\n9676|    \"destination_created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9677|    \"destination_created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:29:58.000Z\",\n9678|    \"destination_extensions\": {},\n9679|    \"member_mappings\": [\n9680|      {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"payments-api\"},\n9681|      {\"source_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_workspace_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\",\"group_relative_path\":\"design-notes\"}\n9682|    ],\n9683|    \"manifest_mappings\": [\n9684|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:7cff7402aa5a31ba0cd7ff9bf49a9dc166b961c9f2b647d1c1084d3e70ce5db8\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:82864b91f66b77e032b5c9aeb86e20091bdf88f6d461e2a26e0d2f4107cfa306\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-3234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7de0-7e55-8e6f-4234567890ab\"},\n9685|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:88d93f20f978b92e75d35e67ebd5a41b90ff1afe106363b05c0f7b08614eb4cf\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:549245f73bff80001d7f2310b06c446124100028e5301083189460b8829a476c\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\"},\n9686|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_tree\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:8dc15e881e026e7cf59482395baaa8c47341e6bad6d87f44312a9d0b360aacd5\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:dd2b8f604b2934127616623b7c70240a6c3acc8e6cdfe6ebdfbf137160abeaaf\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-6cd0-7d44-8d5e-2234567890ab\"},\n9687|      {\"kind\":\"workspace_group\",\"source_manifest_id\":\"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\"destination_manifest_id\":\"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\"source_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\"destination_subject_id\":\"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\"}\n9688|    ]\n9689|  },\n9690|  \"prepared_for_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9691|  \"source_lease_epoch\": 4,\n9692|  \"source_lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n9693|  \"authorities\": [\n9694|    {\"authority_id\":\"workspace_fork\",\"kind\":\"workspace\",\"platform\":\"linux\",\"root_path\":\"/srv/relux-forks\",\"logical_root\":\"relux-forks\",\"workspace_group_id\":\"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\"write_policy\":\"managed_copy\"}\n9695|  ],\n9696|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": null,\n9697|  \"operations\": [\n9698|    {\"sequence\":1,\"action\":\"install_workspace_group\",\"authority_id\":\"workspace_fork\",\"target_relative_path\":\"payments-api-experiment\",\"input_id\":\"sha256:d44fa66c43658f7d4d5613f319c60fea70fbe933dea970f92884e0bb61106ff5\",\"expected_prior_digest\":null,\"atomicity_boundary\":\"target_directory\"}\n9699|  ],\n9700|  \"exclusions\": [\"credential\",\"live_pid\",\"machine_auth\",\"socket\",\"transient_lock\"],\n9701|  \"validations\": [\"manifest_closure\",\"workspace_state\"],\n9702|  \"commit_strategy\": \"atomic_directory_rename\",\n9703|  \"rollback_required\": true,\n9704|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9705|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:29:59.000Z\",\n9706|  \"extensions\": {}\n9707|}\n9708|~~~\n9709|\n9710|The source manifest objects in Section 10.4 are the language-neutral input\n9711|bytes. Applying <code>workspace_fork_v1</code> MUST reproduce all four displayed\n9712|destination IDs: the submodule working tree, Git working tree, managed tree,\n9713|and group root in that order. Implementations MUST compare the fully derived\n9714|JCS bytes, not accept the mapping as an unchecked assertion.\n9715|\n9716|The transaction variants are exact:\n9717|\n9718|| Fixture | Prepare/commit input | Activation and terminal journal |\n9719|| --- | --- | --- |\n9720|| <code>FORK-TXN-DIRECT-NATIVE</code> | The displayed workspace plan, fresh session cohort, empty transfer set | Commit prepares the new workspace; the validated Spawn Plan creates one new native identity; finalize <code>direct_owner_resumed</code> commits the marker and leaves both provider/task-board transaction states <code>none</code> |\n9721|| <code>FORK-TXN-DIRECT-IMPORT</code> | Composite fork plan formed from the same projection plus the exact provider manifest/authority/operation returned for <code>mode=fork</code> | Commit leaves workspace and provider transaction prepared; discovery must find a new identity; finalize commits both only after process proof |\n9722|| <code>FORK-TXN-TASK-BOARD</code> | Composite fork plan formed from the same projection plus the source Task-board Bundle and one fresh task-board staging authority | Commit records import/open with <code>activation_mode=fork</code> and bridge <code>open mode=fork</code>; finalize adopts/resumes the new manager under the new lease, then commits marker and journal |\n9723|\n9724|“Formed from” is the Section 10.5 composite tagged-union operation: it copies\n9725|the displayed source/derived/projection facts and workspace\n9726|authority/operation, unions exactly one permitted provider or task-board\n9727|authority/operation set, sorts authorities/operations/validations, renumbers\n9728|operations consecutively, sets the Plan kind/subject to composite/destination\n9729|session, selects <code>two_phase_multi_root</code>, and recomputes its ID. It is\n9730|not an out-of-band second transaction. In all three rows, a failure before\n9731|activation rolls the one prepared materialization back; a failure after\n9732|process start or adopt is recovered by status/finalize or an explicit fenced\n9733|stop and never by restoring bytes behind a live owner.\n9734|\n9735|The fork Session Record MUST carry those values byte-for-byte for this fixture;\n9736|the <code>fork.created</code> event repeats source/checkpoint/record digest and\n9737|mode so a validator can join provenance without interpreting extensions.\n9738|\n9739|Normative fork Session Record using that provenance:\n9740|\n9741|~~~json\n9742|{\n9743|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n9744|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n9745|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:83c7152b9415c20c90e9009e1fe2e01f9cd3a45ca385b5bc2d678e979756427f\",\n9746|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9747|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-39a0-7a11-8a2b-2234567890ab\",\n9748|  \"name\": \"payments-api-experiment\",\n9749|  \"kind\": \"direct\",\n9750|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:30:00.000Z\",\n9751|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n9752|  \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n9753|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-4ab0-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n9754|  \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n9755|  \"launch_plan\": {\n9756|    \"argv\": [\"codex\"],\n9757|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-5bc0-7c33-8c4d-2234567890ab\",\n9758|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n9759|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n9760|    \"env_literals\": {},\n9761|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n9762|    \"extensions\": {}\n9763|  },\n9764|  \"task_board\": null,\n9765|  \"fork_provenance\": {\n9766|    \"source_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n9767|    \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n9768|    \"source_workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n9769|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-28f0-7900-897a-1234567890ab\",\n9770|    \"provider_fork_mode\": \"native\",\n9771|    \"extensions\": {}\n9772|  },\n9773|  \"extensions\": {}\n9774|}\n9775|~~~\n9776|\n9777|The source lease, provider identity, history, and process are not changed.\n9778|Muse forks with non-empty or active <code>cron.db</code> are unsupported because\n9779|scheduled work could duplicate. Antigravity fork requires the authenticated\n9780|backend's native fork surface; copying local cache/transcripts is not a fork.\n9781|When a provider cannot fork faithfully, the command MUST report\n9782|<code>provider_fork_unsupported</code>; it MUST NOT relabel a blank chat as a\n9783|fork.\n9784|\n9785|Fork failure and recovery are exact:\n9786|\n9787|| Fixture/boundary | Required result |\n9788|| --- | --- |\n9789|| <code>FORK-BEFORE-TOPOLOGY</code> | Validation/allocation failure writes no destination topology, Session Record, lease, provider, or manager |\n9790|| <code>FORK-AFTER-TOPOLOGY</code> | Derived topology/manifests exist but Session Record does not; they remain harmless unreferenced immutable objects eligible for ordinary GC |\n9791|| <code>FORK-AFTER-SESSION</code> | New Session Record and epoch-1 lease exist, but no materialization; state is <code>creating</code> and the same operation may resume at prepare |\n9792|| <code>FORK-MATERIALIZE-NEG</code> | Prepare/commit fails before activation; rollback restores destination, new fork remains failed/creating owner, source is untouched |\n9793|| <code>FORK-DIRECT-IDENTITY-NEG</code> | Provider fork cannot prove a new identity; roll back pre-activation transaction and report <code>provider_fork_unsupported</code>; never use the source or a blank identity |\n9794|| <code>FORK-TB-OPEN-NEG</code> | Import/open fails; journal/status/expiry recovery applies and no manager is adopted |\n9795|| <code>FORK-AFTER-ACTIVATION</code> | Provider/manager is running but finalize response is lost; reconcile status and finalize with the same IDs; byte rollback or a second process is forbidden |\n9796|| <code>FORK-EVENT-LOST</code> | Finalize committed but event publication failed; retry the same event identities and do not recreate topology, lease, provider, or manager |\n9797|\n9798|No fork failure changes the source lease, event chain, provider identity,\n9799|manager binding, workspace marker, or checkpoint. A fork with an authoritative\n9800|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> is non-resumable and remains failed.\n9801|\n9802|### 13.9 Stop\n9803|\n9804|<code>ax stop NAME</code> is graceful by default and executes on the current\n9805|owner, locally or through authenticated <code>session.stop</code> RPC.\n9806|\n9807|Preconditions are a winning owner lease and an available quiesce/stop path.\n9808|Transitions:\n9809|\n9810|1. block input and enter <code>quiescing</code>;\n9811|2. wait for a complete safe boundary;\n9812|3. create and sync a validated checkpoint;\n9813|4. request normal provider/task-board stop;\n9814|5. require process exit and closed durable handles;\n9815|6. if normal exit appended provider/manager closure records, capture and sync a\n9816|   closure-only delta and superseding validated checkpoint; an unexpected\n9817|   workspace/background mutation fails closed while ownership remains local;\n9818|7. record and sync <code>session.stopped</code> with the newest checkpoint; and\n9819|8. retain the same lease, native store, workspace, terminal metadata, and\n9820|   checkpoints.\n9821|\n9822|For a task-board session, steps 1–3 use bridge\n9823|<code>export --mode handoff</code>, step 4 consumes its source-control token\n9824|with bridge <code>stop</code>, and any replacement closure bundle returned in\n9825|step 6 remains opaque. For a direct session, the equivalent actions use the\n9826|provider plugin and terminal backend.\n9827|\n9828|A graceful timeout leaves ownership unchanged and reports\n9829|<code>quiesce_timeout</code> or <code>stop_timeout</code>. The process MAY be\n9830|unquiesced if safe. <code>ax stop NAME --force</code> requires explicit\n9831|confirmation, preserves best-effort diagnostics/checkpoint state, terminates\n9832|the local process, records unclean stop, and does not imply a safe transferable\n9833|checkpoint.\n9834|\n9835|The ordinary successful path returns a non-null final checkpoint,\n9836|<code>resumable=true</code>, <code>bootstrap_aborted=false</code>, and state\n9837|<code>stopped</code>. If the epoch-1 lease has no checkpoint, graceful stop MUST\n9838|either establish the first validated checkpoint and take that ordinary path or\n9839|fail without publishing a stop event. Confirmed force closure in that bootstrap\n9840|window returns a null checkpoint, <code>resumable=false</code>,\n9841|<code>bootstrap_aborted=true</code>, and state <code>failed</code>, after\n9842|publishing the exact two events in Section 13.1. A force stop of a session that\n9843|already has a checkpoint keeps that checkpoint ID, is resumable only from that\n9844|older checkpoint, sets <code>bootstrap_aborted=false</code>, and returns\n9845|<code>stopped</code> only after process/store closure is proved. An unknown\n9846|process or open store handle returns failure and leaves the command retryable;\n9847|it is never represented as a successful closure.\n9848|\n9849|Stop is not delete. Deletion requires a separate future/administrative surface\n9850|that emits a Session Tombstone; v0.3.0 MUST NOT make stop delete state.\n9851|\n9852|### 13.10 Resume\n9853|\n9854|<code>ax resume NAME</code> is allowed only on the winning owner host. A replica\n9855|receives <code>not_owner</code> and explicit attach/takeover/fork choices.\n9856|\n9857|The owner first refreshes lease knowledge and verifies its fencing token. If\n9858|the epoch-1 winning lease has a null checkpoint, resume is not an ordinary\n9859|resume: it executes only the Section 13.1/13.2 bootstrap retry predicate and\n9860|phase continuation. An authoritative bootstrap-abort event returns\n9861|<code>checkpoint_unavailable</code> and cannot be resumed. No later epoch may\n9862|have a null checkpoint.\n9863|\n9864|For a validated checkpoint, derive the exact effective profile/source from its\n9865|event-head closure, probe the mapping/capabilities, and choose exactly one path:\n9866|\n9867|1. <strong>No materialization.</strong> If the current managed marker and native\n9868|   provider/bridge status already equal the checkpoint and winning lease, do\n9869|   not create a transaction. Direct sessions validate native discovery, start\n9870|   <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>, invoke plugin resume with the effective\n9871|   profile, prove the process, and emit <code>session.resumed</code>. A\n9872|   task-board session validates the existing manager binding and calls the\n9873|   public bridge resume with a caller-stable ID/profile, proves status, and\n9874|   emits the event. A missing binding does not qualify for this path.\n9875|2. <strong>Direct materialization.</strong> Call tagged\n9876|   <code>materialize.prepare</code> with <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, the\n9877|   owner as the sole materialization member, empty ownership-transfer set, and\n9878|   workspace/provider/composite kind. Call commit and require durable\n9879|   <code>prepared</code>. Validate native discovery or exact backend identity,\n9880|   start the wrapper, invoke plugin resume, and prove the exact session. Then\n9881|   finalize with <code>direct_owner_resumed</code> and the effective\n9882|   profile/source; only a committed result permits <code>session.resumed</code>.\n9883|3. <strong>Task-board materialization.</strong> Prepare with task-board or\n9884|   composite kind and the same cohort rules. Commit installs the opaque bundle,\n9885|   imports, and opens dormant through the journal. Finalize with\n9886|   <code>task_board_owner_resumed</code>, the winning binding, and effective\n9887|   profile/source; finalize adopts/resumes and proves public bridge status.\n9888|   Only its committed result permits adoption/resume events.\n9889|\n9890|Every materializing path is therefore\n9891|prepare → commit/prepared → identity or dormant validation → activation →\n9892|finalize/committed. A response lost at any arrow is recovered with\n9893|<code>materialize.status</code> plus plugin/bridge status under the same IDs.\n9894|Before direct process start or task-board adopt, validation failure, operator\n9895|abort, or lease loss invokes rollback. After a direct process is proven running\n9896|or task-board adopt succeeds, ordinary byte rollback is forbidden: the same\n9897|owner must finish status/finalize, stop the activation, or perform a new fenced\n9898|ownership operation. Failure leaves the session stopped/failed on that same\n9899|owner and preserves the journal.\n9900|\n9901|Normative resume fixtures are:\n9902|\n9903|| Fixture | Kind/path | Required terminal result |\n9904|| --- | --- | --- |\n9905|| <code>RESUME-NO-MAT-DIRECT</code> | Current workspace/native identity; no transaction | Same lease/profile, exact provider resumed, one resumed event |\n9906|| <code>RESUME-WORKSPACE</code> | Workspace-only prepare/commit, direct native state already current | Marker committed after direct activation; provider transaction remains none |\n9907|| <code>RESUME-PROVIDER</code> | Provider-only prepared transaction | Null marker/path; provider transaction commits only after exact resume |\n9908|| <code>RESUME-COMPOSITE-DIRECT</code> | Workspace plus portable provider | Both roots prepared; exact provider running before finalize cleans backups |\n9909|| <code>RESUME-TASK-BOARD</code> | Task-board-only bundle | Journal opened → adopted → resumed; null marker/path |\n9910|| <code>RESUME-COMPOSITE-TB</code> | Workspace plus bundle | Workspace remains rollbackable until bridge resume proof; then marker/finalize |\n9911|| <code>RESUME-PRE-ACTIVATION-NEG</code> | Any prepared path fails validation | Roll back and remain stopped owner |\n9912|| <code>RESUME-POST-ACTIVATION-NEG</code> | Activation succeeds, response/finalize fails | Status-recover/finalize or explicitly stop; never roll back behind live activation |\n9913|\n9914|It MUST not create a new native session under the old logical identity.\n9915|Antigravity backend <code>not found</code> is\n9916|<code>unsupported_backend_identity</code>, not a successful blank resume.\n9917|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
