{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c671","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":403,"recorded_at":1780531400000801,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"call_id":"call_01a0add09a1e7116afef151bae28be8e","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1769 line(s) above)\n1770|<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,\n1771|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,\n1772|<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,\n1773|<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,\n1774|<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,\n1775|<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,\n1776|<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n1777|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and\n1778|<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.\n1779|\n1780|The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by\n1781|<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a\n1782|member shown as nullable remains required:\n1783|\n1784|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1785|| --- | --- |\n1786|| <code>session.created</code> | <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>first_checkpoint_operation_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n1787|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1788|| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\n1789|| <code>provider.identified</code> | <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak</code> |\n1790|| <code>session.idle</code> | <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code> |\n1791|| <code>session.quiescing</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>reason:graceful_takeover&#124;stop&#124;checkpoint</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code> |\n1792|| <code>checkpoint.created</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>kind:periodic&#124;pre_stop&#124;closure&#124;fork_base&#124;manual</code> |\n1793|| <code>sync.completed</code> | <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>materialized:boolean</code> |\n1794|| <code>session.stopped</code> | <code>graceful:boolean</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>resumable:boolean</code>, <code>closure_kind:checkpointed&#124;bootstrap_abort</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code> |\n1795|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1796|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>failure_phase:before_terminal&#124;after_terminal&#124;after_process&#124;after_identity&#124;before_checkpoint</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>resume_allowed:false</code> |\n1797|| <code>lease.transferred</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>from_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>to_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1798|| <code>lease.forced</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n1799|| <code>session.parked</code> | <code>reason:remote_owner&#124;stale_owner&#124;restore_policy&#124;failed_handoff</code>, <code>winning_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1800|| <code>session.failed</code> | <code>error_code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>retryable:boolean</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n1801|| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1802|| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\n1803|| <code>session.tombstoned</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code> |\n1804|| <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>accepted_risks:sorted unique enum[3]</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1805|| <code>replica.replace_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>expected_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>replacement_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1806|| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\n1807|| <code>task_board.adopted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:digest</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code> |\n1808|| <code>tombstone.issued</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>scope:session&#124;workspace_entry&#124;provider_snapshot&#124;managed_replica</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code> |\n1809|| <code>tombstone.resolved</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>resolution:deleted&#124;already_absent&#124;resurrected&#124;retained_conflict</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>resulting_entry_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1810|\n1811|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1812|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1813|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1814|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1815|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1816|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1817|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1818|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1819|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1820|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1821|null.\n1822|\n1823|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1824|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1825|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1826|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1827|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1828|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1829|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1830|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1831|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1832|\n1833|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1834|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1835|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1836|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1837|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1838|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1839|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1840|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1841|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1842|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1843|\n1844|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1845|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1846|\n1847|Normative example:\n1848|\n1849|~~~json\n1850|{\n1851|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1852|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1853|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1854|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1855|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1856|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1857|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1858|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1859|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1860|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1861|  \"predecessors\": [\n1862|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1863|  ],\n1864|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1865|  \"payload\": {\n1866|    \"graceful\": true,\n1867|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1868|    \"resumable\": true,\n1869|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n1870|    \"process_closed\": true,\n1871|    \"store_closed\": true\n1872|  },\n1873|  \"extensions\": {}\n1874|}\n1875|~~~\n1876|\n1877|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1878|\n1879|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1880|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1881|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1882|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1883|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1884|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c673","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":404,"recorded_at":1780531400000803,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"call_id":"call_01a0add09c4d719ca4970bf878548c52","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(14700 line(s) above)\n14701|## 15. Errors and exit semantics\n14702|\n14703|### 15.1 Structured Error\n14704|\n14705|All machine-readable errors use <code>urn:ax:schema:error</code>. Existing\n14706|Provider/RPC/Bridge and legacy CLI surfaces select version <code>1.0.0</code>,\n14707|whose exact shape is:\n14708|\n14709|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n14710|| --- | --- | --- |\n14711|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Structured Error schema identifier |\n14712|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n14713|| <code>code</code> | string[1..128] | Stable lower-snake-case registry value |\n14714|| <code>message</code> | string[1..4096] | Human text; automation does not branch on it |\n14715|| <code>exit_code</code> | int32 | Exact Section 15.2 code assigned to <code>code</code> |\n14716|| <code>retryable</code> | boolean | True only when the identical request may safely be retried without new authority or confirmation |\n14717|| <code>operation_id</code> | UUIDv7, optional | Present whenever an operation was allocated |\n14718|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7, optional | Present whenever the failure is session-scoped |\n14719|| <code>details</code> | diagnostic data map | Required, redacted open map constrained below |\n14720|\n14721|~~~json\n14722|{\n14723|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:error\",\n14724|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n14725|  \"code\": \"workspace_conflict\",\n14726|  \"message\": \"destination differs from its last materialized checkpoint\",\n14727|  \"exit_code\": 5,\n14728|  \"retryable\": false,\n14729|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-7299-9273-1234567890ab\",\n14730|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n14731|  \"details\": {\n14732|    \"expected_checkpoint\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n14733|    \"remediations\": [\"diff\", \"copy\", \"worktree\", \"replace_managed_replica\"]\n14734|  }\n14735|}\n14736|~~~\n14737|\n14738|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>, <code>code</code>,\n14739|<code>message</code>, <code>exit_code</code>, <code>retryable</code>, and\n14740|<code>details</code> are required. Operation and session IDs are optional and\n14741|MUST be present when known. Messages are for humans; automation MUST branch on\n14742|<code>code</code> and <code>exit_code</code>. Details MUST be redacted and\n14743|schema-valid.\n14744|\n14745|The top-level object is closed. <code>message</code> is 1–4,096 UTF-8\n14746|characters. <code>details</code> is an explicitly open diagnostic data map, not\n14747|an implicit schema extension: it has 0–64 keys matching\n14748|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}</code>, JSON values of maximum nesting depth 4, and\n14749|maximum canonical size 16 KiB. Readers MAY ignore unknown detail keys and MUST\n14750|never infer success, authority, or a remediation action from them. No detail\n14751|may contain a credential, raw transcript, environment secret, or opaque bundle\n14752|content.\n14753|\n14754|Structured Error is independently versioned as a reusable schema, but that\n14755|does not imply independent negotiation inside every envelope. Provider\n14756|protocol <code>2.x</code>, task-board bridge <code>1.x</code>, and Mesh RPC\n14757|<code>2.x</code> each embed exactly Structured Error <code>1.0.0</code>. A\n14758|supported-major failure MUST use that exact object; the containing protocol\n14759|version is sufficient to select it. RPC hello MUST NOT advertise or negotiate\n14760|an <code>error</code> contract key. A future containing-protocol version may\n14761|bind another error version only by stating the new binding explicitly.\n14762|\n14763|Session Adapter 1.0 and <code>session.clone.*</code> bind Structured Error\n14764|1.1.0. It retains the 1.0.0 shape and codes, changes only\n14765|<code>schema_version</code> to exact <code>1.1.0</code>, and adds:\n14766|\n14767|| Exit | Stable clone codes |\n14768|| ---: | --- |\n14769|| 4 | <code>source_not_found</code>, <code>source_ambiguous</code> |\n14770|| 6 | <code>unsupported_environment_tuple</code>, <code>operation_unknown</code>, <code>target_resume_invalid</code> |\n14771|| 9 | <code>source_corrupt</code>, <code>bundle_integrity_failed</code>, <code>credential_material_detected</code> |\n14772|| 11 | <code>source_not_quiescent</code>, <code>source_changed_during_clone</code> |\n14773|| 12 | <code>target_prepare_failed</code>, <code>target_validation_failed</code>, <code>target_checkpoint_failed</code>, <code>transaction_unknown</code> |\n14774|| 13 | <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>, <code>session_adapter_process_failed</code>, <code>session_adapter_timeout</code> |\n14775|| 16 | <code>projection_loss_unacceptable</code>, <code>unsafe_pending_action</code> |\n14776|\n14777|Existing semantically identical codes remain reused. Transaction unknown is a\n14778|parked ambiguous effect, never success or absence. Target checkpoint failure\n14779|occurs only after Provider commit and grants no rollback; the exact inert target\n14780|remains recoverable.\n14781|\n14782|Bootstrap and incompatible-major behavior is exact:\n14783|\n14784|| Surface | Supported-major failure before normal success | Unsupported major or unparseable first frame/output |\n14785|| --- | --- | --- |\n14786|| Provider JSON-over-stdio | A syntactically valid v2 request whose operation/body fails receives the Section 7.2 v2 failure envelope with Error 1.0.0 | The plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2. The host accepts no child error object, terminates/waits for exit as applicable, and emits its own local Error 1.0.0: <code>incompatible_protocol</code> for a recognizable major mismatch, otherwise <code>provider_protocol_error</code> |\n14787|| Task-board bridge facade | A syntactically valid v1 invocation failure receives the Section 9.2 v1 failure envelope with Error 1.0.0 | The facade output is not accepted as a bridge result. <code>ax</code> emits its own local Error 1.0.0: <code>incompatible_protocol</code> for a recognizable major mismatch, otherwise <code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code> |\n14788|| Mesh RPC | Before hello success, a syntactically valid v2 non-hello request or invalid v2 hello receives one v2 failure envelope with Error 1.0.0 and the server then closes | An unsupported protocol major, invalid JSON, oversize line, missing protocol/version/request ID, or response that cannot be framed causes close without an RPC error frame. The initiator emits its own local Error 1.0.0: <code>incompatible_protocol</code> for a recognizable major mismatch, otherwise <code>transport_failure</code> |\n14789|\n14790|A local error above is an <code>ax</code> CLI/observation result, not a forged\n14791|response attributed to the child or peer; it omits unknown operation/session\n14792|IDs and records redacted diagnostics only. Receivers MUST NOT parse a different\n14793|major's payload far enough to trust its error code, retryable bit, details, or\n14794|authority fields.\n14795|\n14796|The normative binding fixtures are\n14797|<code>ERR-PROVIDER-COMPAT</code>, <code>ERR-BRIDGE-COMPAT</code>, and\n14798|<code>ERR-RPC-COMPAT</code>, which use the documented provider/RPC v2 and bridge\n14799|v1 failure envelopes; <code>ERR-PROVIDER-MAJOR</code>,\n14800|<code>ERR-BRIDGE-MAJOR</code>, and <code>ERR-RPC-MAJOR</code>, which change only\n14801|the containing protocol major to 3 for provider/RPC or 2 for the bridge and require the local\n14802|<code>incompatible_protocol</code> result; and\n14803|<code>ERR-PROVIDER-FIRST</code>, <code>ERR-BRIDGE-FIRST</code>, and\n14804|<code>ERR-RPC-FIRST</code>. Provider and RPC fixtures submit valid v2 envelopes\n14805|with an invalid first operation/body and require the bound v2 error; the bridge\n14806|fixture uses its valid v1 invocation and bound v1 error. The RPC fixture submits\n14807|<code>health.get</code> before hello, requires one bound v2 error, and then EOF.\n14808|<code>ERR-FIRST-UNFRAMED</code> supplies invalid JSON to\n14809|each stdio parser (or invalid JSON output from the bridge) and requires no\n14810|remote/child error to be trusted.\n14811|\n14812|### 15.2 Exit codes\n14813|\n14814|| Exit | Meaning |\n14815|| ---: | --- |\n14816|| 0 | Requested operation succeeded |\n14817|| 2 | Usage, invalid flag, or interactive choice required |\n14818|| 3 | Configuration or local precondition invalid |\n14819|| 4 | Session, checkpoint, peer, provider, or task-board identity not found |\n14820|| 5 | Workspace/native-store conflict; no silent overwrite |\n14821|| 6 | Capability unsupported, unknown, conditional, or incompatible |\n14822|| 7 | Authentication/authorization/allowlist failure |\n14823|| 8 | SSH/RPC transport failure; staging can be resumable |\n14824|| 9 | Integrity, schema, hash, or unsafe-path failure |\n14825|| 10 | Ownership/lease/fencing failure |\n14826|| 11 | Busy, quiesce timeout, or graceful stop timeout |\n14827|| 12 | Staging/materialization/rollback failure |\n14828|| 13 | Provider plugin/process failure |\n14829|| 14 | Task-board bridge/bundle/validation failure |\n14830|| 15 | Partial success: immutable sync succeeded but a requested materialization or peer did not |\n14831|| 16 | Explicit policy refusal, including missing destructive confirmation |\n14832|| 17 | Contract/schema migration required |\n14833|| 130 | Interrupted by operator signal before a clean response; inspect authority before retry |\n14834|\n14835|### 15.3 Stable error codes\n14836|\n14837|Protocol 1.0.0 fixes these code-to-exit mappings:\n14838|\n14839|| Exit | Stable error codes |\n14840|| ---: | --- |\n14841|| 2 | <code>interactive_choice_required</code>, <code>invalid_arguments</code> |\n14842|| 3 | <code>invalid_config</code>, <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code> |\n14843|| 4 | <code>name_ambiguous</code>, <code>not_found</code> |\n14844|| 5 | <code>workspace_conflict</code>, <code>native_store_conflict</code> |\n14845|| 6 | <code>capability_unavailable</code>, <code>profile_mapping_unavailable</code>, <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>incompatible_schema</code>, <code>provider_fork_unsupported</code>, <code>unsupported_backend_identity</code> |\n14846|| 7 | <code>authentication_failed</code>, <code>peer_not_allowlisted</code>, <code>host_identity_mismatch</code> |\n14847|| 8 | <code>owner_unreachable</code>, <code>transport_failure</code> |\n14848|| 9 | <code>unsafe_path</code>, <code>integrity_failure</code> |\n14849|| 10 | <code>not_owner</code>, <code>stale_owner</code>, <code>lease_conflict</code>, <code>invalid_state_transition</code> |\n14850|| 11 | <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>workspace_group_busy</code>, <code>workspace_group_changed</code> |\n14851|| 12 | <code>staging_incomplete</code>, <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>, <code>materialization_failed</code>, <code>rollback_failed</code> |\n14852|| 13 | <code>provider_timeout</code>, <code>provider_protocol_error</code>, <code>provider_process_failed</code> |\n14853|| 14 | <code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code>, <code>task_board_bundle_invalid</code>, <code>task_board_validate_failed</code>, <code>checkpoint_unavailable</code> |\n14854|| 15 | <code>partial_sync</code> |\n14855|| 16 | <code>confirmation_required</code>, <code>policy_refused</code>, <code>secret_policy_violation</code> |\n14856|| 17 | <code>migration_required</code> |\n14857|| 130 | <code>interrupted</code> |\n14858|\n14859|New error codes MAY be added in a compatible minor contract version, but an\n14860|unknown code retains the envelope's exit class and MUST NOT be interpreted as\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
