{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e1d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":3911,"recorded_at":1780531400007817,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adec-f253-7de2-8682-55a619513143"},"task_id":"01a0adec-f253-7de2-8682-55a619513143","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adec-f253-7de2-8682-55a619513143","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2623 line(s) above)\n2624|## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n2625|\n2626|[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n2627|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n2628|[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\n2629|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\n2630|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 101\n2631|executable acceptance cases, 56 exact section bindings with their declared\n2632|coverage, 12 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\n2633|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n2634|and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\n2635|The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n2636|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n2637|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n2638|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n2639|\n2640|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n2641|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n2642|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n2643|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n2644|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n2645|build:\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
