{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e2d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":4035,"recorded_at":1780531400008065,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"call_id":"call_01a0adee57d376f4880091af2ea614a2","text":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2709 line(s) above)\n2710|This is what the gate decides, and it is less than semantic coverage. It decides\n2711|that a claimed clause is a real obligation of the claimed section, that it is\n2712|quoted verbatim at the line it occupies, that the discharging acceptance case is\n2713|registered and owned by the binding, and that the declared level equals the\n2714|measured ratio. **It cannot decide that the named acceptance case exercises the\n2715|clause's meaning.** A binding could enumerate every clause of a section and\n2716|point all of them at one weak test, and the gate would admit it. That residual\n2717|class - a complete enumeration discharged by inadequate tests - is not covered\n2718|here and is not claimed to be.\n2719|\n2720|It also cannot see an obligation stated without an RFC 2119 keyword, which is\n2721|why `unmeasured` is refused rather than admitted: the gate reports that it could\n2722|not measure the section instead of inferring that there was nothing to measure.\n2723|And the gap-quality check is a tightening rather than a proof - a sentence that\n2724|names both its section and its production declaration and still says nothing\n2725|useful is admitted, and the gate cannot decide otherwise.\n2726|\n2727|### Measured coverage of this repository\n2728|\n2729|`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\n2730|\n2731|```text\n2732|section coverage: bindings=56 full=1 partial=3 sliver=1 unevidenced=48 unmeasured=3 unowned=12 clauses_discharged=17/463\n2733|```\n2734|\n2735|Fifty-six section bindings discharge 17 of the 463 normative clauses their\n2736|sections carry. One binding is `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n2737|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\n2738|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\n2739|with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
