{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e451","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":4227,"recorded_at":1780531400008449,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adef-02fc-7e43-a763-71b612409fc7"},"task_id":"01a0adef-02fc-7e43-a763-71b612409fc7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adef-02fc-7e43-a763-71b612409fc7","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1752 line(s) above)\n1753|[`internal/sessstate`](internal/sessstate) derives deterministic logical-session\n1754|state from the immutable records (pinned v0.5.0 Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2, 5.7,\n1755|14.4): every `SessionState` value, the winning lease epoch, lease conflicts,\n1756|the current checkpoint, provider identity, and terminal binding. `Reduce` is a\n1757|pure function of its input — record facts plus the authoritative events in\n1758|chain order — performing no I/O and keeping no cache, so the same event\n1759|sequence always yields the same state. `Project` binds the pure core to one\n1760|`sessrepo.Repository`: it locates the session through `ListSessions`, loads\n1761|the stored record and chain through `GetRecord`, `ListEvents`, and `GetEvent`,\n1762|and folds them through `Reduce`. It only reads and owns no crash window; its\n1763|idempotency is the reducer's purity, pinned by projecting twice and requiring\n1764|byte-equal results.\n1765|\n1766|The Section 5.7 transition table is the single source the step gate enforces:\n1767|a same-state restatement is not a transition, the first event may only open a\n1768|bootstrap state, and every other move needs its table edge, else\n1769|`invalid_state_transition`. Chain continuity is re-checked over the reducer\n1770|input, so a chain-forbidden reordering refuses instead of silently deriving a\n1771|different state. The winning lease is the greatest `(epoch, lease_id)` tuple\n1772|over the chain leases and the union leases; a same-epoch tie resolves to the\n1773|bytewise-greater lease ID, an epoch gap keeps the greatest tuple while\n1774|recording the gap, losing union branches report preserved-never-applied, and\n1775|an off-chain union winner moves the reported winner without rewriting\n1776|authoritative state — each as reported conflict data under its named rule,\n1777|never as an error. An empty chain derives creating, but its union still passes\n1778|through the same validation: a malformed union refuses exactly as on a\n1779|non-empty chain, while a well-formed union moves only the reported winner.\n1780|Without an authoritative event, `Local` is ignored, including malformed and\n1781|partial tuples; it is not validated and changes no state, winner, conflict or\n1782|warning. `LocalHostID` leaves the role unknown even with a selected union\n1783|winner. `TestReduceEmptyChainLocalIsIgnored` pins this bound through `Reduce`.\n1784|Takeover while the winner is active stales the old host's\n1785|projection exactly where the table lets it go stale; a local lease that lost\n1786|the tuple rule stales the local projection the same way. No event derives\n1787|stopped while the newest checkpoint is null, the failed-to-creating retry\n1788|requires epoch 1 under the create lease with no checkpoint and no abort, and\n1789|`task_board.launched` must repeat the creation lease and the record provider\n1790|or fail integrity. A parked session from `sessrepo` reaches `SessionState` as\n1791|the parked state carrying its blocking reason and retry — never as an error\n1792|or an omission — and the listing tells a parked name apart from a missing one\n1793|with no repository interface change.\n1794|\n1795|Decode projects members from attested bytes and never re-attests: canonical\n1796|identity stays single-owned at the `sessrepo` durable boundary (pinned by the\n1797|provhost no-attestation-outside-the-leaf gate), so `DecodeRecord` and\n1798|`DecodeEvent` check frame and member grammars through their owners and read\n1799|the grammar-checked self member instead of recomputing a digest.\n1800|\n1801|The package resolves no names, renders no list/status output, and takes no\n1802|interactive choice: the full Section 2.3 order with choice and Section 14.4\n1803|rendering belong to the sibling name-resolution leaf. It adds no `ax`\n1804|command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim.\n1805|\n1806|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n1807|\n1808|```bash\n1809|go test ./internal/sessstate -count=1\n1810|go test ./internal/sessstate -cover -count=1\n1811|```\n1812|\n1813|The unfiltered package run derives the 69-site refusal inventory from the\n1814|production source through `internal/invcore` (39 in `sessstate.go`, 28 in\n1815|`decode.go`, 2 in `project.go`): every `refuse` call site must have a\n1816|boundary-driven negative path (`Reduce`, `DecodeRecord`, `DecodeEvent`,\n1817|`Project`), every exercised site must derive, sentinel wraps outside the\n1818|funnel fail, and the observed sentinel set must equal the derived roster. A\n1819|second derived census covers the 11 `SessionState` spellings — structurally\n1820|derived from the `State`-typed const block, each living exactly once as a\n1821|production literal, each driven to through the production `Reduce` entry —\n1822|and a third covers the 24 handled v1 event types derived from direct-selector\n1823|switches and comparisons against the pinned Section 5.2 registry, each row\n1824|naming its lifecycle-or-fact class and driver. `TestEventTypeUsesAreOwned`\n1825|adds the ownership prerequisite: every production `Type` selector, including\n1826|ones in new files or package bindings, must match one of four exact AST use\n1827|contexts. Copies, helper arguments, address-taking and other unregistered\n1828|contexts fail closed, as do orphan rows, duplicate uses and unclassifiable\n1829|sites. This is direct-field-access ownership, not whole-program taint\n1830|analysis: reflective/unsafe/serialization access to whole `Event` values and\n1831|later interpretation of permitted diagnostic strings remain unproved.\n1832|Unrelated selectors named `Type` also need classification.\n1833|\n1834|The alias audit keeps the funnel and watched owner delegations\n1835|(`DecodeStrictObject`, `CheckUUIDv7`, `CheckUint53Bounds`, `ParseDigest`,\n1836|`ParseUUIDv4`, `ParseProviderID`, `ParseID`) in direct-call position, with\n1837|import-alias and var-binding controls. Named `TestSessstateStaticAudit`\n1838|exposes this layer separately. The task outcome records the selected mutation\n1839|battery with disjoint behavioral, census and static-audit selectors; a\n1840|census failure is never reported as a behavioral kill. The selected mutants\n1841|cover reduce/read/recovery paths; this package owns no durable write path.\n1842|Their count is not a claim that every possible dispatch or mutation is covered.\n1843|\n1844|`TestCensusLiveEventOwnershipPlants` compiles and wires direct-switch PA,\n1845|var-binding PB, string-helper PC and pointer-neighbor PD through `Reduce`.\n1846|All four fail the census; their unchanged behavioral-suite result is reported\n1847|separately. Independent control-effect probes are added only after the\n1848|shipped layers run and do not count as shipped behavioral kills. Neutral XN\n1849|survives (identity-transform bound); known-bad XK fails the unknown-v1\n1850|behavioral test. The gate's own narrowing that admits only the simple\n1851|`kind := event.Type` copy is killed by the live PB control. Run this focused\n1852|composition with:\n1853|\n1854|```bash\n1855|go test ./internal/sessstate -count=1 -run '^TestCensusLiveEventOwnershipPlants$' -v\n1856|```\n1857|\n1858|The live test uses a temporary package copy and read-only dependency symlinks;\n1859|it restores its copied sources and never mutates the managed worktree. It runs\n1860|on the normal package suite and adds compiler/subprocess time. Task validation\n1861|logs and mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-1r9wrr`; scratch\n1862|outputs live under `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/`.\n1863|\n1864|## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans\n1865|\n1866|`internal/sessquery` is the single shared selector API over the persisted\n1867|session repositories and the accepted state projector. It implements the\n1868|v0.6.0 selector contract (§14.7/§14.7.1, refining §2.3) with shared\n1869|SelectionPlan construction and revalidation (§14.7.2):\n1870|\n1871|- Literal grammar: split at the first `@` only. The key is a NAME, a bare\n1872|  UUID (name-first precedence kept), or `id:UUID` (bypasses names for the\n1873|  durable union identity). The source is empty (bare §2.3 tiers), `local`,\n1874|  `peer:ALIAS` (the entire remaining suffix, literal — spaces, `@`,\n1875|  Unicode, and `%` included), or `id:HOST_UUID`. No joining, aliasing,\n1876|  percent-decoding, Unicode normalization, trimming, or alias folding.\n1877|- Exact source mappings: effective configuration (local host, peer\n1878|  alias/host mappings, allowlist) is validated first, including exact\n1879|  alias and host-ID uniqueness; duplicates are `invalid_config`.\n1880|  Explicit unknown aliases/hosts are `selector_source_not_found`; known\n1881|  but disallowed peers are `peer_not_allowlisted`. Remote read failures\n1882|  are `selector_source_read_failed` with the cause preserved; local I/O\n1883|  keeps its repository error; malformed authority is `integrity_failure`.\n1884|- No explicit-source fallback: a qualified key resolves in its one\n1885|  source only. Tier, collision, and tombstone semantics follow §14.7.1:\n1886|  exact live name then UUID-shaped name within the source, replicated\n1887|  copies deduplicate only on agreeing record digests (else\n1888|  `integrity_failure`), distinct colliding names refuse with\n1889|  `name_ambiguous`, and tombstoned entries stay excluded on\n1890|  authoritative tombstone evidence while failed reads never count as it.\n1891|- Immutable plans: `Reader.BuildPlan` binds all sixteen §14.7.2\n1892|  members — the literal selector, session and validated record digest,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
