{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e5ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":4401,"recorded_at":1780531400008797,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adf0-0684-7940-a1a4-0c4d64539aa2"},"task_id":"01a0adf0-0684-7940-a1a4-0c4d64539aa2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adf0-0684-7940-a1a4-0c4d64539aa2","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-17\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-2f5393 — implement Lease Record validation and CAS lifecycle\n9|- SCOPE (`internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go`): epoch-1 `create` leases from\n10|  the durable bootstrap inputs, successor leases through compare-and-swap,\n11|  fencing-token renewal, the operational grant-expiry policy, epoch\n12|  monotonicity (head plus one, never from input), host-UUIDv7 holder\n13|  identity, and tuple-ordered reads over content-addressed blobs with no\n14|  lease index to skew. Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10 (v0.6.0).\n15|- DESIGN: no second lease model — closed shape/identity stay with\n16|  `canonicaljson`, the tuple rule stays with `sessstate.Compare`\n17|  (restated as `CompareLeaseTuple` across the import cycle, pinned by a\n18|  cross-package agreement test), and `sessquery.winningLeaseFor` is\n19|  unchanged (an adoption test proves store-minted records admit there).\n20|  Mint failures are plain operational errors, never refusals, so a\n21|  weakened grammar gate fails closed at mint with a changed class —\n22|  which is what kills its narrowing mutant.\n23|- EXPIRY POLICY: the lease itself never expires (Section 5.3; pinned by\n24|  an ancient-`created_at` test); only the process-local fencing grant\n25|  lapses past the configured refresh interval, and revalidation renews\n26|  it. Grants are never persisted or replicated.\n27|- CAS IDEMPOTENCY: a retry names its pre-commit basis, so the replay\n28|  check re-mints against that basis (not the head) and answers the\n29|  persisted successor; this fixed a real bug found by the idempotency\n30|  test where head-minted retries minted epoch+2 and tripped token reuse.\n31|- CRASH: injector arms (`safe_retry` pre-write, `recoverable_parked`\n32|  post-commit with replay) plus real SIGKILL child drills at the\n33|  stage-then-rename seam for create and CAS, with fresh-handle reopen,\n34|  orphaned-temp tolerance, and exact-epoch retry assertions.\n35|- MUTANTS: the shipped `internal/sessrepo/testdata/mutate.py` battery\n36|  reports 27/27 applied plants killed (26 narrowing — one per new\n37|  `refuse` site — plus 1 token-preserving timestamp mutant); the\n38|  harmless control is `SURVIVED`,\n39|  `NOT_APPLIED`/`COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE` stay separate. The refusal\n40|  census grows to 61 sites (26 lease) and the equality census to three\n41|  ledgered sites.\n42|- COVERAGE: 8 of 8 shared-library AC rows driven by named production\n43|  entries; public CLI coverage is 0 of 8 by stated ownership bound.\n44|  Candidate left uncommitted in the managed Story worktree for handoff.\n45|\n46|### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\n47|- REVIEW FINDING CLOSED (CR15 P2-A): the package-wide `go/types` census\n48|  compared lexical `*types.TypeName` objects, so a Go alias could bypass the\n49|  sealed `checkpointSeal`/`checkpointSealToken` inventory. The initial alias\n50|  baseline admitted the direct, token, chained, and container plants; its\n51|  recorded exit was 1 before the fix.\n52|- FIX (`internal/sessquery/rev11_regression_test.go`): every sealed type and\n53|  value identity path now applies `types.Unalias` before canonical comparison\n54|  and before structural descent. The recursive coverage includes chained\n55|  aliases, pointers, arrays, slices, maps, channels, structs, function\n56|  signatures, generic arguments, interfaces, type parameters, and unions.\n57|  Unrelated named capability types are not opened through their underlying\n58|  representation, so the census keeps the public capability boundary intact.\n59|- TESTS (`internal/sessquery/rev15_regression_test.go`): direct, chained,\n60|  container, and function-signature alias plants all refuse through the same\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
