ncludes chained\n55|  aliases, pointers, arrays, slices, maps, channels, structs, function\n56|  signatures, generic arguments, interfaces, type parameters, and unions.\n57|  Unrelated named capability types are not opened through their underlying\n58|  representation, so the census keeps the public capability boundary intact.\n59|- TESTS (`internal/sessquery/rev15_regression_test.go`): direct, chained,\n60|  container, and function-signature alias plants all refuse through the same\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
