{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ea5f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcf-af6f-7db0-8726-470499e8596b"},"sequence":5002,"recorded_at":1780531400009999,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3b578cbb-cd1c-4970-859d-8c242cd48356"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\n`TASK-260830-3g12yp` is `to-review` with 14/14 checklist items and three outcome artifacts attached (`results.md`, `conformance-matrix.md`, `producer-evidence.tar.gz`). The candidate is uncommitted in the Story worktree as required.\n\nWhat was built: `internal/fencing` gates all five activation-class actions (activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, restore) plus terminate-stale on the winning lease and exact epoch, with launch-class park decisions carrying the `session.parked` vocabulary and a sealed `LeaseToken` for quiesce/capture/materialize. No second lease model: winner loads through `sessrepo`, expiry reuses `CheckFencingExpiry`, and every refusal carries a Section 15 registered code only (proven through `axerror`). 18 of 18 AC rows are driven by named tests at named production entries.\n\nEvidence: 40 fencing tests green at 97.5% coverage; mutant battery 31/31 killed (30 narrowing + 1 token-preserving census mutant run against the full suite); full repo suite 27 packages ok; race, vet, gofmt, Windows build/vet, and tracecheck all clean. Traceability: 5.3 moved to the real `CompareAndSwapLease` owner (7/8 partial), 2.2 moved from unowned to a 4/22 sliver, 9 lease acceptance cases registered, pin re-derived (110/57/28/485), and the tuple-agreement test extended to an exhaustive 144-pair enumeration.","reason":null}}
